// TypeScript 5.9 (and the ECMAScript 2025 it includes) as the TypeScript 5.9 compiler's parser accepts it,
// parsed into a typed AST modeled on the compiler's: each type is named after the SyntaxKind of its node.
// The start rule main parses a .ts file, or a .tsx file (JSX instead of <T>x type assertions) when the input
// starts with the character NUL (U+0000), which no TypeScript file can start with: the Go package prepends it
// for ParseTSX and moves the positions back, so that one generated parser serves both. After it, U+0001 parses
// the top level in the await context, as the compiler reparses the statements of a module that contain await
// (ParseFile does it for modules).
//
// The grammar follows the compiler's parser (src/compiler/parser.ts) function by function, so that it
// accepts what the parser accepts without a syntactic diagnostic: it is as lenient as the parser is (most
// "grammar errors" are reported by the checker and are not syntax errors here), and it decides the
// ambiguities the way the parser does (arrow functions, type arguments in expressions, <T>x and JSX,
// contextual keywords, automatic semicolon insertion).
//
// Whitespace. Rules do not skip whitespace around themselves, so that every node spans exactly its tokens;
// the caller skips what may come before. ws skips any whitespace and comments; sp skips them without
// crossing a line terminator (a /* */ comment containing one counts as a line terminator). Where the
// compiler checks scanner.hasPrecedingLineBreak() (ASI, restricted productions, contextual keywords), the
// grammar uses sp, or nl to test for a line break before the next token.
//
// Context. The parser's context flags are kept in one int variable, ctx, as a set of bits:
//     1 yield context, 2 await context, 4 disallow `in`, 8 decorator context,
//     16 no return type on arrow functions (allowReturnTypeInArrowFunction = false),
//     32 disallow conditional types, 64 JSX (a .tsx file).
// One variable rather than seven: rules that read variables are memoized per value, and each read and
// definition walks the variable environment, so a single variable keeps both cheap.
// Tests are written [ctx / 4 % 2 == 1] (bit 4 set); a bit b is cleared with ctx - ctx / b % 2 * b.
//
// Performance. The grammar follows the compiler's order of alternatives, which tries what is rare before what is
// common, and a rule that fails at once still costs a call and records what it expected. What paid, measured
// as rule calls (pego profile) and as time on the benchmarks of the package (see the README):
//   - A silent lookahead of the next character in front of an alternative or an operator (&(?...)), which
//     records no expectation: the operators of binaryExpression and the postfix operators of the
//     left-hand side, whose Pratt loops try every operator after every operand; the ws and sp rules, which
//     are called twice a token; the modifiers, the unary operators and the update expressions.
//   - Dispatch by the first character or word: primaryExpression and nonArrayType try identifiers and type
//     references first (they are the most common, and cannot be mistaken for a keyword); the statements that
//     start with a keyword, a brace, ";" or "@" are apart from expression statements; assignmentExpressionInner
//     tests for each of its alternatives; reservedWord tests the first letter.
//   - One parse where the compiler's order parsed twice and relied on the memo: a union, an intersection or a
//     conditional type, and a conditional expression, are a fold over the optional tail of their first operand
//     (the same for ++ and --) instead of an alternative that parses the operand, fails and parses it again.
//   - No rule call per character of an identifier (identifierRest).
// Together they take the rule calls on 300 KB of the TypeScript compiler's own JavaScript from 1.66 M to 0.59 M,
// and the parse time of lib.dom.d.ts and of the compiler to about half.
// What did not pay: ws and sp matching one character at a time inside a lookahead, and ordering the alternatives
// of statement by frequency.
// The #error labels of primaryExpression and nonArrayType replace the long lists of tokens the silent tests no
// longer record by "expected an expression" and "expected a type"; they cost nothing measurable.
package typescript

// ===================================================================
// Types
// ===================================================================

// --- Terminals ---
type Identifier terminal
type PrivateIdentifier terminal
type Token terminal                          // a punctuation or keyword token (QuestionToken, PlusToken, ...)
type Modifier terminal                       // a modifier keyword (ExportKeyword, ...)
type KeywordTypeNode terminal                // any, number, void, ... (AnyKeyword, NumberKeyword, ...)
type ThisTypeNode terminal                   // this as a type (ThisType)
type NumericLiteral terminal
type BigIntLiteral terminal
type StringLiteral terminal                  // with its quotes
type RegularExpressionLiteral terminal
type NoSubstitutionTemplateLiteral terminal  // with its backquotes
type TemplateHead terminal                   // from ` to ${
type TemplateMiddle terminal                 // from } to ${
type TemplateTail terminal                   // from } to `
type ThisExpression terminal                 // ThisKeyword
type SuperExpression terminal                // SuperKeyword
type NullLiteral terminal                    // NullKeyword
type BooleanLiteral terminal                 // TrueKeyword or FalseKeyword
type ImportExpression terminal               // ImportKeyword, the callee of import(...)
type OmittedExpression terminal              // an empty slot of an array literal or pattern
type JsxText terminal
type JsxOpeningFragment terminal
type JsxClosingFragment terminal
type EmptyStatement terminal
type DebuggerStatement terminal
type SemicolonClassElement terminal
type EndOfFileToken terminal
type JSDocAllType terminal
type JSDocUnknownType terminal

// --- Names ---
type QualifiedName struct { Left EntityName, Right Identifier }
type ComputedPropertyName struct { Expression Expression }

// --- Signature elements ---
type TypeParameter struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name Identifier, Constraint *TypeNode, Default *TypeNode
    Expression *Expression  // a constraint that is an expression (extends +1), which the checker reports
}
type Parameter struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, DotDotDotToken *Token, Name *BindingName, QuestionToken *Token  // Name is nil only in JSDoc function types
    Type *TypeNode, Initializer *Expression
}
type Decorator struct { Expression Expression }

// --- Type members ---
type PropertySignature struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name PropertyName, QuestionToken *Token, Type *TypeNode, Initializer *Expression
}
type MethodSignature struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name PropertyName, QuestionToken *Token, TypeParameters []TypeParameter
    Parameters []Parameter, Type *TypeNode
}
type CallSignature struct { TypeParameters []TypeParameter, Parameters []Parameter, Type *TypeNode }
type ConstructSignature struct { TypeParameters []TypeParameter, Parameters []Parameter, Type *TypeNode }
type IndexSignature struct { Modifiers []ModifierLike, Parameters []Parameter, Type *TypeNode }

// --- Class members ---
type PropertyDeclaration struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name PropertyName, QuestionToken *Token, ExclamationToken *Token
    Type *TypeNode, Initializer *Expression
}
type MethodDeclaration struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, AsteriskToken *Token, Name PropertyName, QuestionToken *Token
    ExclamationToken *Token, TypeParameters []TypeParameter, Parameters []Parameter, Type *TypeNode, Body *Block
}
type ClassStaticBlockDeclaration struct { Modifiers []ModifierLike, Body Block }
type Constructor struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, TypeParameters []TypeParameter, Parameters []Parameter, Type *TypeNode, Body *Block
}
type GetAccessor struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name PropertyName, TypeParameters []TypeParameter, Parameters []Parameter
    Type *TypeNode, Body *Block
}
type SetAccessor struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name PropertyName, TypeParameters []TypeParameter, Parameters []Parameter
    Type *TypeNode, Body *Block
}

// --- Types ---
type TypePredicate struct { AssertsModifier *Token, ParameterName TypePredicateParameterName, Type *TypeNode }
type TypeReference struct { TypeName EntityName, TypeArguments []TypeNode }
type FunctionType struct { TypeParameters []TypeParameter, Parameters []Parameter, Type TypeNode }
type ConstructorType struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, TypeParameters []TypeParameter, Parameters []Parameter, Type TypeNode
}
type TypeQuery struct { ExprName EntityName, TypeArguments []TypeNode }
type TypeLiteral struct { Members []TypeElement }
type ArrayType struct { ElementType TypeNode }
type TupleType struct { Elements []TypeNode }
type OptionalType struct { Type TypeNode }
type RestType struct { Type TypeNode }
type UnionType struct { Types []TypeNode }
type IntersectionType struct { Types []TypeNode }
type ConditionalType struct { CheckType TypeNode, ExtendsType TypeNode, TrueType TypeNode, FalseType TypeNode }
type InferType struct { TypeParameter TypeParameter }
type ParenthesizedType struct { Type TypeNode }
type TypeOperator struct { Operator string, Type TypeNode }  // Operator is keyof, unique or readonly
type IndexedAccessType struct { ObjectType TypeNode, IndexType TypeNode }
type MappedType struct {
    ReadonlyToken *Token, TypeParameter TypeParameter, NameType *TypeNode, QuestionToken *Token
    Type *TypeNode, Members []TypeElement
}
type LiteralType struct { Literal LiteralTypeLiteral }
type NamedTupleMember struct { DotDotDotToken *Token, Name Identifier, QuestionToken *Token, Type TypeNode }
type TemplateLiteralType struct { Head TemplateHead, TemplateSpans []TemplateLiteralTypeSpan }
type TemplateLiteralTypeSpan struct { Type TypeNode, Literal TemplateMiddleOrTail }
type ImportType struct {
    Argument TypeNode, Attributes *ImportAttributes, Qualifier *EntityName, TypeArguments []TypeNode
    IsTypeOf bool
}
type JSDocNullableType struct { Type TypeNode, Postfix bool }
type JSDocNonNullableType struct { Type TypeNode, Postfix bool }
type JSDocFunctionType struct { Parameters []Parameter, Type *TypeNode }

// --- Binding patterns ---
type ObjectBindingPattern struct { Elements []BindingElement }
type ArrayBindingPattern struct { Elements []ArrayBindingElement }
type BindingElement struct {
    DotDotDotToken *Token, PropertyName *PropertyName, Name BindingName, Initializer *Expression
}

// --- Expressions ---
type ArrayLiteralExpression struct { Elements []Expression }
type ObjectLiteralExpression struct { Properties []ObjectLiteralElement }
type PropertyAssignment struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name PropertyName, QuestionToken *Token, ExclamationToken *Token
    Initializer Expression
}
type ShorthandPropertyAssignment struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name Identifier, QuestionToken *Token, ExclamationToken *Token
    EqualsToken *Token, ObjectAssignmentInitializer *Expression
}
type SpreadAssignment struct { Expression Expression }
type PropertyAccessExpression struct { Expression Expression, QuestionDotToken *Token, Name MemberName }
type ElementAccessExpression struct { Expression Expression, QuestionDotToken *Token, ArgumentExpression Expression }
type CallExpression struct {
    Expression Expression, QuestionDotToken *Token, TypeArguments []TypeNode, Arguments []Expression
}
type NewExpression struct { Expression Expression, TypeArguments []TypeNode, Arguments *[]Expression }  // Arguments is nil without parentheses
type TaggedTemplateExpression struct {
    Tag Expression, QuestionDotToken *Token, TypeArguments []TypeNode, Template TemplateLiteral
}
type TypeAssertionExpression struct { Type TypeNode, Expression Expression }
type ParenthesizedExpression struct { Expression Expression }
type FunctionExpression struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, AsteriskToken *Token, Name *Identifier, TypeParameters []TypeParameter
    Parameters []Parameter, Type *TypeNode, Body Block
}
type ArrowFunction struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, TypeParameters []TypeParameter, Parameters []Parameter, Type *TypeNode
    EqualsGreaterThanToken Token, Body ConciseBody
}
type DeleteExpression struct { Expression Expression }
type TypeOfExpression struct { Expression Expression }
type VoidExpression struct { Expression Expression }
type AwaitExpression struct { Expression Expression }
type PrefixUnaryExpression struct { Operator string, Operand Expression }
type PostfixUnaryExpression struct { Operand Expression, Operator string }
type BinaryExpression struct { Left Expression, OperatorToken Token, Right Expression }
type ConditionalExpression struct {
    Condition Expression, QuestionToken Token, WhenTrue Expression, ColonToken Token, WhenFalse Expression
}
type TemplateExpression struct { Head TemplateHead, TemplateSpans []TemplateSpan }
type TemplateSpan struct { Expression Expression, Literal TemplateMiddleOrTail }
type YieldExpression struct { AsteriskToken *Token, Expression *Expression }
type SpreadElement struct { Expression Expression }
type ClassExpression struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name *Identifier, TypeParameters []TypeParameter
    HeritageClauses []HeritageClause, Members []ClassElement
}
type ExpressionWithTypeArguments struct { Expression Expression, TypeArguments []TypeNode }
type AsExpression struct { Expression Expression, Type TypeNode }
type SatisfiesExpression struct { Expression Expression, Type TypeNode }
type NonNullExpression struct { Expression Expression }
type MetaProperty struct { KeywordToken string, Name Identifier }  // KeywordToken is new or import

// --- JSX ---
type JsxElement struct { OpeningElement JsxOpeningElement, Children []JsxChild, ClosingElement JsxClosingElement }
type JsxSelfClosingElement struct { TagName JsxTagName, TypeArguments []TypeNode, Attributes JsxAttributes }
type JsxOpeningElement struct { TagName JsxTagName, TypeArguments []TypeNode, Attributes JsxAttributes }
type JsxClosingElement struct { TagName JsxTagName }
type JsxFragment struct {
    OpeningFragment JsxOpeningFragment, Children []JsxChild, ClosingFragment JsxClosingFragment
}
type JsxAttributes struct { Properties []JsxAttributeLike }
type JsxAttribute struct { Name JsxAttributeName, Initializer *JsxAttributeValue }
type JsxSpreadAttribute struct { Expression Expression }
type JsxExpression struct { DotDotDotToken *Token, Expression *Expression }
type JsxNamespacedName struct { Namespace Identifier, Name Identifier }

// --- Statements ---
type SourceFile struct { Statements []Statement, EndOfFileToken EndOfFileToken }
type Block struct { Statements []Statement }
type VariableStatement struct { Modifiers []ModifierLike, DeclarationList VariableDeclarationList }
type VariableDeclarationList struct { Keyword string, Declarations []VariableDeclaration }  // var, let, const, using or await using
type VariableDeclaration struct {
    Name BindingName, ExclamationToken *Token, Type *TypeNode, Initializer *Expression
}
type ExpressionStatement struct { Expression Expression }
type IfStatement struct { Expression Expression, ThenStatement Statement, ElseStatement *Statement }
type DoStatement struct { Statement Statement, Expression Expression }
type WhileStatement struct { Expression Expression, Statement Statement }
type ForStatement struct {
    Initializer *ForInitializer, Condition *Expression, Incrementor *Expression, Statement Statement
}
type ForInStatement struct { Initializer ForInitializer, Expression Expression, Statement Statement }
type ForOfStatement struct {
    AwaitModifier *Token, Initializer ForInitializer, Expression Expression, Statement Statement
}
type ContinueStatement struct { Label *Identifier }
type BreakStatement struct { Label *Identifier }
type ReturnStatement struct { Expression *Expression }
type WithStatement struct { Expression Expression, Statement Statement }
type SwitchStatement struct { Expression Expression, CaseBlock CaseBlock }
type CaseBlock struct { Clauses []CaseOrDefaultClause }
type CaseClause struct { Expression Expression, Statements []Statement }
type DefaultClause struct { Statements []Statement }
type LabeledStatement struct { Label Identifier, Statement Statement }
type ThrowStatement struct { Expression Expression }
type TryStatement struct { TryBlock Block, CatchClause *CatchClause, FinallyBlock *Block }
type CatchClause struct { VariableDeclaration *VariableDeclaration, Block Block }

// --- Declarations ---
type FunctionDeclaration struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, AsteriskToken *Token, Name *Identifier, TypeParameters []TypeParameter
    Parameters []Parameter, Type *TypeNode, Body *Block
}
type ClassDeclaration struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name *Identifier, TypeParameters []TypeParameter
    HeritageClauses []HeritageClause, Members []ClassElement
}
type HeritageClause struct { Token string, Types []ExpressionWithTypeArguments }  // Token is extends or implements
type InterfaceDeclaration struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name Identifier, TypeParameters []TypeParameter
    HeritageClauses []HeritageClause, Members []TypeElement
}
type TypeAliasDeclaration struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name Identifier, TypeParameters []TypeParameter, Type TypeNode
}
type EnumDeclaration struct { Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name Identifier, Members []EnumMember }
type EnumMember struct { Name PropertyName, Initializer *Expression }
type ModuleDeclaration struct { Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name ModuleName, Body *ModuleBody }
type ModuleBlock struct { Statements []Statement }
type NamespaceExportDeclaration struct { Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name Identifier }
type ImportEqualsDeclaration struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, Name Identifier, ModuleReference ModuleReference, IsTypeOnly bool
}
type ExternalModuleReference struct { Expression Expression }
type ImportDeclaration struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, ImportClause *ImportClause, ModuleSpecifier Expression
    Attributes *ImportAttributes
}
type ImportClause struct { Name *Identifier, NamedBindings *NamedImportBindings, PhaseModifier string }  // PhaseModifier is type, defer or empty
type NamespaceImport struct { Name Identifier }
type NamedImports struct { Elements []ImportSpecifier }
type ImportSpecifier struct { PropertyName *ModuleExportName, Name Identifier, IsTypeOnly bool }
type ImportAttributes struct { Elements []ImportAttribute, Token string }  // Token is with or assert
type ImportAttribute struct { Name ImportAttributeName, Value Expression }
type ExportAssignment struct { Modifiers []ModifierLike, Expression Expression, IsExportEquals bool }
type ExportDeclaration struct {
    Modifiers []ModifierLike, ExportClause *NamedExportBindings, ModuleSpecifier *Expression
    Attributes *ImportAttributes, IsTypeOnly bool
}
type NamedExports struct { Elements []ExportSpecifier }
type NamespaceExport struct { Name ModuleExportName }
type ExportSpecifier struct { PropertyName *ModuleExportName, Name ModuleExportName, IsTypeOnly bool }

// --- Unions ---
type EntityName = Identifier | QualifiedName
type PropertyName = Identifier | StringLiteral | NumericLiteral | BigIntLiteral | ComputedPropertyName
    | PrivateIdentifier | NoSubstitutionTemplateLiteral
type MemberName = Identifier | PrivateIdentifier
type BindingName = Identifier | ObjectBindingPattern | ArrayBindingPattern
type ArrayBindingElement = BindingElement | OmittedExpression
type ModifierLike = Modifier | Decorator
type TypePredicateParameterName = Identifier | ThisTypeNode
type LiteralTypeLiteral = StringLiteral | NumericLiteral | BigIntLiteral | BooleanLiteral | NullLiteral
    | PrefixUnaryExpression | NoSubstitutionTemplateLiteral
type TemplateMiddleOrTail = TemplateMiddle | TemplateTail
type TemplateLiteral = NoSubstitutionTemplateLiteral | TemplateExpression
type TypeNode = KeywordTypeNode | ThisTypeNode | TypePredicate | TypeReference | FunctionType | ConstructorType
    | TypeQuery | TypeLiteral | ArrayType | TupleType | OptionalType | RestType | UnionType | IntersectionType
    | ConditionalType | InferType | ParenthesizedType | TypeOperator | IndexedAccessType | MappedType
    | LiteralType | NamedTupleMember | TemplateLiteralType | ImportType | JSDocAllType | JSDocUnknownType
    | JSDocNullableType | JSDocNonNullableType | JSDocFunctionType
type TypeElement = CallSignature | ConstructSignature | PropertySignature | MethodSignature | IndexSignature
    | GetAccessor | SetAccessor
type ClassElement = PropertyDeclaration | MethodDeclaration | Constructor | SemicolonClassElement | GetAccessor
    | SetAccessor | IndexSignature | ClassStaticBlockDeclaration
type ObjectLiteralElement = PropertyAssignment | ShorthandPropertyAssignment | SpreadAssignment
    | MethodDeclaration | GetAccessor | SetAccessor
type Expression = Identifier | PrivateIdentifier | NumericLiteral | BigIntLiteral | StringLiteral
    | RegularExpressionLiteral | NoSubstitutionTemplateLiteral | TemplateExpression | ThisExpression
    | SuperExpression | NullLiteral | BooleanLiteral | ImportExpression | OmittedExpression
    | ArrayLiteralExpression | ObjectLiteralExpression | PropertyAccessExpression | ElementAccessExpression
    | CallExpression | NewExpression | TaggedTemplateExpression | TypeAssertionExpression
    | ParenthesizedExpression | FunctionExpression | ArrowFunction | DeleteExpression | TypeOfExpression
    | VoidExpression | AwaitExpression | PrefixUnaryExpression | PostfixUnaryExpression | BinaryExpression
    | ConditionalExpression | YieldExpression | SpreadElement | ClassExpression | ExpressionWithTypeArguments
    | AsExpression | SatisfiesExpression | NonNullExpression | MetaProperty | JsxElement
    | JsxSelfClosingElement | JsxFragment
type ConciseBody = Block | Expression
type Statement = Block | EmptyStatement | VariableStatement | ExpressionStatement | IfStatement | DoStatement
    | WhileStatement | ForStatement | ForInStatement | ForOfStatement | ContinueStatement | BreakStatement
    | ReturnStatement | WithStatement | SwitchStatement | LabeledStatement | ThrowStatement | TryStatement
    | DebuggerStatement | FunctionDeclaration | ClassDeclaration | InterfaceDeclaration
    | TypeAliasDeclaration | EnumDeclaration | ModuleDeclaration | ImportEqualsDeclaration
    | ImportDeclaration | ExportAssignment | ExportDeclaration | NamespaceExportDeclaration
type ForInitializer = VariableDeclarationList | Expression
type CaseOrDefaultClause = CaseClause | DefaultClause
type ModuleName = Identifier | StringLiteral
type ModuleBody = ModuleBlock | ModuleDeclaration
type ModuleReference = Identifier | QualifiedName | ExternalModuleReference
type NamedImportBindings = NamespaceImport | NamedImports
type NamedExportBindings = NamedExports | NamespaceExport
type ModuleExportName = Identifier | StringLiteral
type ImportAttributeName = Identifier | StringLiteral
type JsxChild = JsxText | JsxExpression | JsxElement | JsxSelfClosingElement | JsxFragment
type JsxAttributeLike = JsxAttribute | JsxSpreadAttribute
type JsxAttributeName = Identifier | JsxNamespacedName
type JsxAttributeValue = StringLiteral | JsxExpression | JsxElement | JsxSelfClosingElement | JsxFragment
type JsxTagName = Identifier | ThisExpression | JsxNamespacedName | PropertyAccessExpression
type JsxTagNameStart = Identifier | ThisExpression

// ===================================================================
// Source files
// ===================================================================

def main: SourceFile = ("\u{0}" [ctx = 64] / [ctx = 0]) ("\u{1}" [ctx = ctx + 2])? f:sourceFile -> $f

def sourceFile: SourceFile = hashbang? -ws ss:(s:topLevelStatement -ws)* e:endOfFile
    -> new SourceFile{Statements: map($ss, (x) => $x.s), EndOfFileToken: $e}
// When the top level is in the await context (a module, see main), the compiler reparses only the statements
// that may contain await: not import and export declarations, enums and namespaces, which keep the script's
// context (their await is an identifier).
def topLevelStatement: Statement = awaitFreeTopLevelStatement / otherTopLevelStatement
def otherTopLevelStatement: Statement = !([ctx / 2 % 2 == 1] topLevelAwaitFreeStart) s:statement -> $s
def awaitFreeTopLevelStatement: Statement = [ctx / 2 % 2 == 1] &topLevelAwaitFreeStart [ctx = ctx - 2] s:statement
    -> $s
def topLevelAwaitFreeStart = (modifierKeyword -ws)* ("import" !idPart !(-ws (?(.))
    / "export" !idPart -ws (("type" !idPart -ws)? (?=*{) / ("default" / "as") !idPart)
    / ("enum" / "namespace" / "module" / "global") !idPart)
def endOfFile: EndOfFileToken = $$
def hashbang = "#!" (?^\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029})*

// ===================================================================
// Statements (parseStatement)
// ===================================================================

// The keyword decides; the contextual keywords of declarations (type, namespace, declare, ...) start a
// declaration only when isStartOfDeclaration says so, and an expression statement otherwise.
def statement: Statement = (&statementSpecialStart s:specialStatement / !statementSpecialStart s:plainStatement)
    -> $s
// A statement that starts with a brace, ";", "@", a keyword or a contextual keyword of declarations (which may also
// start an expression). If none of them matches, the statement is not tried as a plain one (a block followed by
// "=" is an error, not an expression statement).
def specialStatement: Statement = block / emptyStatement / variableStatement / plainFunctionDeclaration
    / plainClassDeclaration / ifStatement / doStatement / whileStatement / forStatement / continueStatement / breakStatement
    / returnStatement / withStatement / switchStatement / throwStatement / tryStatement / debuggerStatement
    / decoratedDeclaration / contextualDeclaration / expressionOrLabeledStatement
def statementSpecialStart = (?{;@) / &(?abcdefgilmnoprstuvw) (statementKeyword / declarationKeyword) !idPart
def statementKeyword = "var" / "let" / "using" / "await" / "function" / "class" / "if" / "do" / "while" / "for"
    / "continue" / "break" / "return" / "with" / "switch" / "throw" / "try" / "debugger"
// Any other statement is an expression statement or a labeled statement.
def plainStatement: Statement = s:(labeledStatement / expressionStatement) -> $s
def plainFunctionDeclaration: FunctionDeclaration = &("function" !idPart) d:functionDeclaration -> $d
def plainClassDeclaration: ClassDeclaration = &("class" !idPart) d:classDeclaration -> $d
def decoratedDeclaration: Statement = &"@" d:declaration -> $d
def contextualDeclaration: Statement = &(declarationKeyword !idPart) &declarationStart d:declaration -> $d
def declarationKeyword = "async" / "interface" / "type" / "module" / "namespace" / "declare" / "const" / "enum"
    / "export" / "import" / "private" / "protected" / "public" / "abstract" / "accessor" / "static" / "readonly"
    / "global"

// "=" after a block is an error (parseBlock): {a} = b is not a destructuring assignment.
def block: Block = "{" -ws ss:(s:statement -ws)* "}" !(-ws "=" !(?=>)) -> new Block{Statements: map($ss, (x) => $x.s)}
def emptyStatement: EmptyStatement = ";"

// var, let x, using x and await using x without modifiers (isLetDeclaration, isUsingDeclaration, ...)
def variableStatement: VariableStatement = &variableStatementStart l:variableDeclarationList eos
    -> new VariableStatement{DeclarationList: $l}
def variableStatementStart = "var" !idPart / "let" !idPart letFollows / "using" !idPart usingFollows
    / "await" !idPart -ws "using" !idPart usingFollows
// let declares before an identifier or a pattern, on any line
def letFollows = -ws (bindingIdentifier / (?[{))
// using declares before an identifier or {, on the same line
def usingFollows = sp (bindingIdentifier / "{")

def ifStatement: IfStatement = "if" !idPart -ws "(" -ws e:expressionAllowIn -ws ")" -ws t:statement
    (-ws "else" !idPart -ws s:statement)?
    -> new IfStatement{Expression: $e, ThenStatement: $t, ElseStatement: $s}
// The ";" after do-while is optional, without automatic semicolon insertion.
def doStatement: DoStatement = "do" !idPart -ws s:statement -ws "while" !idPart -ws "(" -ws e:expressionAllowIn
    -ws ")" (-ws ";")? -> new DoStatement{Statement: $s, Expression: $e}
def whileStatement: WhileStatement = "while" !idPart -ws "(" -ws e:expressionAllowIn -ws ")" -ws s:statement
    -> new WhileStatement{Expression: $e, Statement: $s}
def withStatement: WithStatement = "with" !idPart -ws "(" -ws e:expressionAllowIn -ws ")" -ws s:statement
    -> new WithStatement{Expression: $e, Statement: $s}

// for, for-in, for-of and for await (parseForOrForInOrForOfStatement)
def forStatement: Statement = forOfStatement / forInStatement / forClassicStatement
def forOfStatement: ForOfStatement = "for" !idPart (-ws t:awaitToken)? -ws "(" -ws i:forInitializer -ws
    "of" !idPart -ws e:assignmentExpressionAllowIn -ws ")" -ws s:statement
    -> new ForOfStatement{AwaitModifier: $t, Initializer: $i, Expression: $e, Statement: $s}
def forInStatement: ForInStatement = "for" !idPart -ws "(" -ws i:forInitializer -ws "in" !idPart -ws
    e:expressionAllowIn -ws ")" -ws s:statement
    -> new ForInStatement{Initializer: $i, Expression: $e, Statement: $s}
def forClassicStatement: ForStatement = "for" !idPart -ws "(" -ws i:forInitializer? -ws ";" -ws
    c:expressionAllowIn? -ws ";" -ws n:expressionAllowIn? -ws ")" -ws s:statement
    -> new ForStatement{Initializer: $i, Condition: $c, Incrementor: $n, Statement: $s}
def awaitToken: Token = "await" !idPart
// The initializer is parsed with `in` disallowed, so that for (x in y) is a for-in statement.
def forInitializer: ForInitializer = [ctx = ctx - ctx / 4 % 2 * 4 + 4] i:(forDeclarationList / expression) -> $i
def forDeclarationList: VariableDeclarationList = &(("var" / "let" / "const") !idPart
        / "using" !idPart forUsingFollows / "await" !idPart -ws "using" !idPart usingFollows)
    l:variableDeclarationList -> $l
// using of is a declaration before =, ; or : (disallowOf)
def forUsingFollows = -ws "of" !idPart -ws (?=;:) / sp !("of" !idPart) (bindingIdentifier / "{")

def continueStatement: ContinueStatement = "continue" !idPart (!canParseSemicolon -ws n:identifier)? eos
    -> new ContinueStatement{Label: $n}
def breakStatement: BreakStatement = "break" !idPart (!canParseSemicolon -ws n:identifier)? eos
    -> new BreakStatement{Label: $n}
def returnStatement: ReturnStatement = "return" !idPart (!canParseSemicolon -ws e:expressionAllowIn)? eos
    -> new ReturnStatement{Expression: $e}
def throwStatement: ThrowStatement = "throw" !idPart (!nlAhead -ws e:expressionAllowIn / &nlAhead &(-ws e:missingIdentifier))
    (eos / [text($e) == "declare"]) -> new ThrowStatement{Expression: $e}
def missingIdentifier: Identifier = _
def debuggerStatement: DebuggerStatement = "debugger" !idPart eos

def switchStatement: SwitchStatement = "switch" !idPart -ws "(" -ws e:expressionAllowIn -ws ")" -ws b:caseBlock
    -> new SwitchStatement{Expression: $e, CaseBlock: $b}
def caseBlock: CaseBlock = "{" -ws cs:(c:caseOrDefaultClause -ws)* "}"
    -> new CaseBlock{Clauses: map($cs, (x) => $x.c)}
def caseOrDefaultClause: CaseOrDefaultClause = caseClause / defaultClause
def caseClause: CaseClause = "case" !idPart -ws e:expressionAllowIn -ws ":" ss:(-ws s:clauseStatement)*
    -> new CaseClause{Expression: $e, Statements: map($ss, (x) => $x.s)}
def defaultClause: DefaultClause = "default" !idPart -ws ":" ss:(-ws s:clauseStatement)*
    -> new DefaultClause{Statements: map($ss, (x) => $x.s)}
def clauseStatement: Statement = !(("case" / "default") !idPart) s:statement -> $s

def tryStatement: TryStatement = "try" !idPart -ws b:block (-ws cc:catchClause)?
    (-ws "finally" !idPart -ws fb:block)? [$cc != nil || $fb != nil]
    -> new TryStatement{TryBlock: $b, CatchClause: $cc, FinallyBlock: $fb}
def catchClause: CatchClause = "catch" !idPart (-ws "(" -ws d:variableDeclaration -ws ")")? -ws b:block
    -> new CatchClause{VariableDeclaration: $d, Block: $b}

// An expression statement, or a labeled statement if the expression is an identifier followed by ":"
// (parseExpressionOrLabeledStatement).
// An expression statement does not start with "{", "@", function or class (isStartOfExpressionStatement).
def expressionOrLabeledStatement: Statement = !(&(declarationKeyword !idPart) declarationStart)
    !variableStatementStart !((?{@) / ("function" / "class") !idPart)
    s:(labeledStatement / expressionStatement / declareStatement) -> $s
def labeledStatement: LabeledStatement = &((?a-zA-Z$_\\\u{80}-\u{10FFFF}) identifierRest -ws ":") l:identifier -ws ":" -ws s:statement
    -> new LabeledStatement{Label: $l, Statement: $s}
def expressionStatement: ExpressionStatement = e:expressionAllowIn eos -> new ExpressionStatement{Expression: $e}
// The identifier declare needs no terminator: the parser reports no missing ";" after it
// (parseErrorForMissingSemicolonAfter), and goes on with the next statement on the same line.
def declareStatement: ExpressionStatement = &(x:expressionAllowIn) [text($x) == "declare"] e:declareIdentifier
    -> new ExpressionStatement{Expression: $e}
def declareIdentifier: Identifier = "declare" !idPart

// A statement terminator (parseSemicolon): ";", or nothing before a line break, "}" or the end of input.
def eos = -ws ";" / &canParseSemicolon
def canParseSemicolon = sp ((?;}\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}) / "/*" / $$)
// A line break before the next token: sp stops at a line terminator, or at a /* */ comment containing one.
def nlAhead = sp ((?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}) / "/*")

// ===================================================================
// Declarations (isStartOfDeclaration, parseDeclaration)
// ===================================================================

// isDeclaration: modifiers on the same line followed by a declaration keyword.
// (declarationStart and typeStart recurse at the end, after a modifier or "(", so pego lint hints that a Document
// would evaluate them again after an edit; they are lookaheads over a few tokens of a generated parser.)
def declarationStart = ("var" / "let" / "const" / "function" / "class" / "enum") !idPart
    / "using" !idPart usingFollows
    / "await" !idPart -ws "using" !idPart usingFollows
    / ("interface" / "type" / "defer") !idPart sp identifier
    / ("module" / "namespace") !idPart sp (identifier / (?"'))
    / "declare" !idPart sp "type" !idPart
    / ("abstract" / "accessor" / "async" / "declare" / "private" / "protected" / "public" / "readonly") !idPart
        !nlAhead -ws declarationStart
    / "global" !idPart -ws ("{" / !anyKeyword identifierName / "export" !idPart)
    / "import" !idPart -ws ("defer" !idPart / (?"'*{#) / idStart)
    / "export" !idPart -ws ("type" !idPart -ws)? ((?=*{@) / ("default" / "as") !idPart)
    / "export" !idPart -ws declarationStart
    / "static" !idPart -ws declarationStart

def declaration: Statement = variableStatementWithModifiers / functionDeclaration / classDeclaration
    / interfaceDeclaration / typeAliasDeclaration / enumDeclaration / moduleDeclaration
    / importEqualsDeclaration / importDeclaration / exportAssignment / namespaceExportDeclaration
    / exportDeclaration

def variableStatementWithModifiers: VariableStatement = m:modifiers
    &(("var" / "let" / "const" / "using") !idPart / "await" !idPart -ws "using" !idPart)
    l:variableDeclarationList eos -> new VariableStatement{Modifiers: $m, DeclarationList: $l}

// --- Variables ---
// for (let of x) declares nothing (canFollowContextualOfKeyword).
def variableDeclarationList: VariableDeclarationList = k:declarationListKeyword
    (!(-ws "of" !idPart -ws identifier -ws ")") -ws d:variableDeclarations
        / &(-ws "of" !idPart -ws identifier -ws ")") / !(-ws ((?{[#) / bindingIdentifier)))
    -> new VariableDeclarationList{Keyword: text($k), Declarations: concat($d)}
def declarationListKeyword = @(("var" / "let" / "const" / "using") !idPart / "await" -ws "using" !idPart)
def variableDeclarations = first:variableDeclaration rest:(-ws "," -ws d:variableDeclaration)*
    (-ws "," !(-ws ((?{[#) / bindingIdentifier)))?
    -> concat(list($first), map($rest, (r) => $r.d))
// The definite assignment x! is not parsed in a for initializer (where `in` is disallowed).
def variableDeclaration: VariableDeclaration =
    (n:bindingIdentifier ([ctx / 4 % 2 == 0] -sp x:exclamationToken)? / n:bindingPattern) ty:typeAnnotation?
    (!(-ws ("in" / "of") !idPart) v:initializer)?
    -> new VariableDeclaration{Name: $n, ExclamationToken: $x, Type: $ty, Initializer: $v}
def initializer = -ws "=" !(?=>) -ws e:assignmentExpression -> $e
def typeAnnotation = -ws ":" -ws t:typeNode -> $t

// --- Binding patterns ---
def bindingName: BindingName = bindingIdentifier / bindingPattern
def bindingPattern: BindingName = objectBindingPattern / arrayBindingPattern
def objectBindingPattern: ObjectBindingPattern = "{" -ws [ctx = ctx - ctx / 4 % 2 * 4]
    es:bindingElementList? -ws "}"
    -> new ObjectBindingPattern{Elements: concat($es)}
def bindingElement: BindingElement = bindingElementWithPropertyName / bindingElementShorthand
def bindingElementWithPropertyName: BindingElement = (t:dotDotDotToken -ws)? p:propertyName -ws ":" -ws
    n:bindingName i:initializer?
    -> new BindingElement{DotDotDotToken: $t, PropertyName: $p, Name: $n, Initializer: $i}
def bindingElementShorthand: BindingElement = (t:dotDotDotToken -ws)? n:bindingName i:initializer?
    -> new BindingElement{DotDotDotToken: $t, Name: $n, Initializer: $i}
def arrayBindingPattern: ArrayBindingPattern = "[" -ws [ctx = ctx - ctx / 4 % 2 * 4]
    es:arrayBindingElementList? -ws "]"
    -> new ArrayBindingPattern{Elements: concat($es)}
def arrayBindingElement: ArrayBindingElement = omittedExpression / bindingElementShorthand
def omittedExpression: OmittedExpression = &","

// --- Functions ---
// The name may be left out only with the default modifier (export default function () {}). The
// parameters and the body are parsed in the yield context of a generator and the await context of an
// async function.
def functionDeclaration: FunctionDeclaration = (&(dm:defaultModifierScan))? (&(am:asyncModifierScan))?
    m:modifiers "function" !idPart (-ws s:asteriskToken)? (-ws i:bindingIdentifier)? [$i != nil || $dm != nil]
    [ctx = ctx - ctx % 32 + len($s) + len($am) / 5 * 2]
    (-ws t:typeParameters)? -ws ps:parameterList rt:returnType? (-ws fb:block / !(-ws "{") eos)
    -> new FunctionDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, AsteriskToken: $s, Name: $i, TypeParameters: concat($t),
        Parameters: $ps, Type: $rt, Body: $fb}
def defaultModifierScan = (!("default" !idPart) (decorator / modifier / staticModifier) -ws)* d:@("default" !idPart)
    -> $d
def asyncModifierScan = (!("async" !idPart) (decorator / modifier / staticModifier) -ws)* a:@("async" !idPart)
    -> $a

def parameterList = "(" -ws ps:parameters? -ws ")" -> concat($ps)
def parameters = first:parameter rest:(-ws "," -ws p:parameter)* (-ws ",")?
    -> concat(list($first), map($rest, (r) => $r.p))
def parameter: Parameter = thisParameter / regularParameter
def thisParameter: Parameter = n:thisIdentifier t:typeAnnotation? -> new Parameter{Name: $n, Type: $t}
def thisIdentifier: Identifier = "this" !idPart
def regularParameter: Parameter = m:modifiers (dt:dotDotDotToken -ws)? n:bindingName (-ws qt:questionToken)?
    t:typeAnnotation? i:initializer?
    -> new Parameter{Modifiers: $m, DotDotDotToken: $dt, Name: $n, QuestionToken: $qt, Type: $t, Initializer: $i}
// A return type allows conditional types again (allowConditionalTypesAnd).
def returnType = -ws ":" -ws [ctx = ctx - ctx / 32 % 2 * 32] t:typeOrTypePredicate -> $t

// --- Classes ---
def classDeclaration: ClassDeclaration = m:modifiers "class" !idPart (-ws i:className)?
    (-ws t:typeParameters)? (-ws hc:heritageClauses)? -ws "{" -ws ms:classMembers "}"
    -> new ClassDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, Name: $i, TypeParameters: concat($t), HeritageClauses: concat($hc),
        Members: $ms}
def classExpression: ClassExpression = m:modifiers "class" !idPart (-ws i:className)?
    (-ws t:typeParameters)? (-ws hc:heritageClauses)? -ws "{" -ws ms:classMembers "}"
    -> new ClassExpression{Modifiers: $m, Name: $i, TypeParameters: concat($t), HeritageClauses: concat($hc),
        Members: $ms}
// class implements X {} has no name (isImplementsClause)
def className: Identifier = !("implements" !idPart -ws idStart) i:bindingIdentifier -> $i

def heritageClauses = first:heritageClause rest:(-ws h:heritageClause)*
    -> concat(list($first), map($rest, (r) => $r.h))
def heritageClause: HeritageClause = t:@(("extends" / "implements") !idPart)
    (&(-ws heritageElementStart) -ws l:heritageTypes / !(-ws heritageElementStart))
    -> new HeritageClause{Token: text($t), Types: concat($l)}
// isListElement for HeritageClauseElement
def heritageElementStart = "{" -ws !("}" !(-ws ((?,{) / ("extends" / "implements") !idPart)))
    / !"{" !(("extends" / "implements") !idPart -ws expressionStart) leftHandSideExpressionStart
// isStartOfLeftHandSideExpression
def leftHandSideExpressionStart = (?0-9"'`([{/) / "." (?0-9)
    / ("this" / "super" / "null" / "true" / "false" / "function" / "class" / "new") !idPart
    / "import" !idPart -ws (?(<.)
    / !reservedWord idStart
def heritageTypes = first:expressionWithTypeArguments rest:(-ws "," -ws e:expressionWithTypeArguments)*
    (-ws "," !(-ws heritageElementStart))?
    -> concat(list($first), map($rest, (r) => $r.e))
// An element is a left-hand side expression and its type arguments; {} is an element only before
// ",", "{", extends or implements (isValidHeritageClauseObjectLiteral).
def expressionWithTypeArguments: ExpressionWithTypeArguments =
    !(("extends" / "implements") !idPart -ws expressionStart)
    !("{" -ws "}" !(-ws ((?,{) / ("extends" / "implements") !idPart)))
    e:heritageExpression (-ws t:typeArguments)?
    -> new ExpressionWithTypeArguments{Expression: $e, TypeArguments: concat($t)}

def classMembers = ms:(&(classMemberStart / ";") m:classElement -ws)* -> map($ms, (x) => $x.m)
// isClassMemberStart: a decorator, a class member modifier (public, static, ...) after other modifiers, "*",
// "[", or a name; a keyword (other than get and set) or a modifier taken for a name only before what can
// follow a property or method name.
def classMemberStart = "@"
    / (nonMemberModifier -ws)* (memberModifier / (?*[) / literalPropertyNameToken -ws "["
        / ("get" / "set") !idPart / !anyKeyword literalPropertyNameToken
        / literalPropertyNameToken classMemberNameFollows)
    / nonMemberModifier (-ws nonMemberModifier)* classMemberNameFollows
def nonMemberModifier = ("abstract" / "async" / "const" / "declare" / "default" / "export" / "in" / "out") !idPart
def memberModifier = ("public" / "private" / "protected" / "readonly" / "static" / "override" / "accessor") !idPart
def classMemberNameFollows = -ws (?(<!:=?) / canParseSemicolon
def classElement: ClassElement = semicolonClassElement / classStaticBlock / classAccessor / classMemberNotAccessor
def classAccessor: ClassElement = &(classModifiers accessorKeyword) m:(getAccessor / setAccessor) -> $m
def classMemberNotAccessor: ClassElement = !(classModifiers accessorKeyword)
    m:(constructorDeclaration / classIndexSignature / methodDeclaration / propertyDeclaration) -> $m
// get or set before a name: an accessor
def accessorKeyword = ("get" / "set") !idPart &(-ws canFollowGetOrSet)
def semicolonClassElement: SemicolonClassElement = ";"
def classStaticBlock: ClassStaticBlockDeclaration = m:classModifiers "static" !idPart -ws &"{"
    [ctx = ctx - ctx % 32 + 2] b:block -> new ClassStaticBlockDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, Body: $b}
def getAccessor: GetAccessor = m:classModifiers "get" !idPart &(-ws canFollowGetOrSet) -ws n:propertyName
    [ctx = ctx - ctx % 32] (-ws t:typeParameters)? -ws ps:parameterList rt:returnType? (-ws fb:block / !(-ws "{") eos)
    -> new GetAccessor{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps, Type: $rt, Body: $fb}
def setAccessor: SetAccessor = m:classModifiers "set" !idPart &(-ws canFollowGetOrSet) -ws n:propertyName
    [ctx = ctx - ctx % 32] (-ws t:typeParameters)? -ws ps:parameterList rt:returnType? (-ws fb:block / !(-ws "{") eos)
    -> new SetAccessor{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps, Type: $rt, Body: $fb}
def canFollowGetOrSet = "[" / literalPropertyNameStart
// A constructor is named constructor, or "constructor" before "(" (parseConstructorName).
def constructorDeclaration: Constructor = m:classModifiers constructorName [ctx = ctx - ctx % 32]
    (-ws t:typeParameters)? -ws ps:parameterList rt:returnType? (-ws fb:block / !(-ws "{") eos)
    -> new Constructor{Modifiers: $m, TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps, Type: $rt, Body: $fb}
def constructorName = "constructor" !idPart / ("\"constructor\"" / "'constructor'") &(-ws "(")
def classIndexSignature: IndexSignature = m:classModifiers &indexSignatureStart "[" -ws ps:parameters? -ws "]"
    t:typeAnnotation? typeMemberSemicolon
    -> new IndexSignature{Modifiers: $m, Parameters: concat($ps), Type: $t}
// A method has "*", or "(" or "<" after its name; anything else named is a property
// (parsePropertyOrMethodDeclaration).
def methodDeclaration: MethodDeclaration = (&(am:asyncModifierScan))? m:classModifiers !constructorName
    (s:asteriskToken -ws)? n:propertyName (-ws qt:questionToken)? ([$s != nil] / &(-ws (?(<)))
    [ctx = ctx - ctx % 32 + len($s) + len($am) / 5 * 2]
    (-ws t:typeParameters)? -ws ps:parameterList rt:returnType? (-ws fb:block / !(-ws "{") eos)
    -> new MethodDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, AsteriskToken: $s, Name: $n, QuestionToken: $qt,
        TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps, Type: $rt, Body: $fb}
// The initializer is parsed outside the yield and await contexts, with `in` allowed; "@" or "(" on the
// same line after the property is an error (parseSemicolonAfterPropertyName).
def propertyDeclaration: PropertyDeclaration = m:classModifiers !constructorName n:propertyName
    (-ws qt:questionToken / -sp x:exclamationToken)? t:typeAnnotation?
    (-ws "=" !(?=>) -ws [ctx = ctx - ctx % 8] v:assignmentExpression)? !(-sp (?@()) eos
    -> new PropertyDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, QuestionToken: $qt, ExclamationToken: $x, Type: $t,
        Initializer: $v}

// --- Interfaces, type aliases, enums ---
def interfaceDeclaration: InterfaceDeclaration = m:modifiers "interface" !idPart -ws n:identifier
    (-ws t:typeParameters)? (-ws hc:heritageClauses)? -ws ms:objectTypeMembers
    -> new InterfaceDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, TypeParameters: concat($t), HeritageClauses: concat($hc),
        Members: $ms}
// type T = intrinsic declares an intrinsic type (tryParse(parseKeywordAndNoDot)).
def typeAliasDeclaration: TypeAliasDeclaration = m:modifiers "type" !idPart !nlAhead -ws n:identifier
    (-ws t:typeParameters)? -ws "=" -ws ty:(intrinsicKeyword / typeNode) eos
    -> new TypeAliasDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, TypeParameters: concat($t), Type: $ty}
def intrinsicKeyword: KeywordTypeNode = "intrinsic" !idPart !(-ws ".")
def enumDeclaration: EnumDeclaration = m:modifiers "enum" !idPart -ws n:identifier -ws "{" -ws
    [ctx = ctx - ctx % 4] ms:enumMemberList? -ws "}"
    -> new EnumDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, Members: concat($ms)}
def enumMember: EnumMember = n:propertyName (-ws "=" !(?=>) -ws v:assignmentExpressionAllowIn)?
    -> new EnumMember{Name: $n, Initializer: $v}

// --- Modules ---
def moduleDeclaration: ModuleDeclaration = namespaceDeclaration / externalModuleDeclaration / globalDeclaration
def namespaceDeclaration: ModuleDeclaration = m:modifiers ("namespace" / "module") !idPart -ws n:identifier
    b:namespaceBody -> new ModuleDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, Body: $b}
def namespaceBody: ModuleBody = (-ws "." -ws d:nestedNamespace / -ws d:moduleBlock) -> $d
def nestedNamespace: ModuleDeclaration = n:identifierNameOrPrivate b:namespaceBody -> new ModuleDeclaration{Name: $n, Body: $b}
def externalModuleDeclaration: ModuleDeclaration = m:modifiers "module" !idPart -ws n:stringLiteral
    (-ws mb:moduleBlock / eos) -> new ModuleDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, Body: $mb}
def globalDeclaration: ModuleDeclaration = m:modifiers n:globalIdentifier (-ws mb:moduleBlock / eos)
    -> new ModuleDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, Body: $mb}
def globalIdentifier: Identifier = "global" !idPart
def moduleBlock: ModuleBlock = "{" -ws ss:(s:statement -ws)* "}" -> new ModuleBlock{Statements: map($ss, (x) => $x.s)}

// --- Imports ---
// import x = require("m"), import type x = N.M
def importEqualsDeclaration: ImportEqualsDeclaration = m:modifiers "import" !idPart -ws
    (tt:"type" !idPart -ws &identifier)? n:identifier -ws "=" !(?=>) -ws r:moduleReference eos
    -> new ImportEqualsDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, ModuleReference: $r, IsTypeOnly: $tt != nil}
def moduleReference: ModuleReference = externalModuleReference / entityName
def externalModuleReference: ExternalModuleReference = "require" !idPart -ws "(" -ws e:moduleSpecifier -ws ")"
    -> new ExternalModuleReference{Expression: $e}
def importDeclaration: ImportDeclaration = m:modifiers "import" !idPart -ws
    (ic:importClause -ws "from" !idPart -ws / "defer" !idPart -ws !(identifier / (?*{,=)) / !identifier !(?*{))
    s:moduleSpecifier (-sp at:importAttributes)? eos
    -> new ImportDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, ImportClause: $ic, ModuleSpecifier: $s, Attributes: $at}
// The phase modifier: import type ... and import defer ... (parseImportDeclarationOrImportEqualsDeclaration)
def importClause: ImportClause = (pk:importPhase -ws)? (n:identifier (-ws "," -ws b:namedImportBindings)?
        / b:namedImportBindings)
    -> new ImportClause{Name: $n, NamedBindings: $b, PhaseModifier: text($pk)}
def importPhase = @("type" !idPart &(-ws ("from" !idPart -ws ("from" !idPart / "=" !"=")
        / !("from" !idPart) (identifier / (?*{))))
    / "defer" !idPart &(-ws ("from" !idPart !(-ws (?"')) / !("from" !idPart) !(?,=))))
def namedImportBindings: NamedImportBindings = namespaceImport / namedImports
def namespaceImport: NamespaceImport = "*" -ws "as" !idPart -ws n:identifier -> new NamespaceImport{Name: $n}
def namedImports: NamedImports = "{" -ws es:importSpecifierList? -ws "}"
    -> new NamedImports{Elements: concat($es)}
// The type modifier and as (parseImportOrExportSpecifier): type as as x, type as x, type as, type x as y, x as y
def importSpecifier: ImportSpecifier = importSpecifierTypeAsAs / importSpecifierTypeAsName / importSpecifierTypeAs
    / importSpecifierType / importSpecifierPlain
def importSpecifierTypeAsAs: ImportSpecifier = "type" !idPart -ws p:asIdentifier -ws "as" !idPart -ws n:importedName
    -> new ImportSpecifier{PropertyName: $p, Name: $n, IsTypeOnly: true}
def importSpecifierTypeAsName: ImportSpecifier = p:typeIdentifier -ws "as" !idPart -ws n:importedName
    -> new ImportSpecifier{PropertyName: $p, Name: $n}
def importSpecifierTypeAs: ImportSpecifier = "type" !idPart -ws n:asIdentifier !(-ws moduleExportNameStart)
    -> new ImportSpecifier{Name: $n, IsTypeOnly: true}
def importSpecifierType: ImportSpecifier = "type" !idPart -ws &moduleExportNameStart
    (p:moduleExportName -ws "as" !idPart -ws n:importedName / n:importedName)
    -> new ImportSpecifier{PropertyName: $p, Name: $n, IsTypeOnly: true}
def importSpecifierPlain: ImportSpecifier = (p:moduleExportName -ws "as" !idPart -ws n:importedName / n:importedName)
    -> new ImportSpecifier{PropertyName: $p, Name: $n}
def typeIdentifier: Identifier = "type" !idPart
def importedName: Identifier = identifier / privateName
def privateName: Identifier = "#" ((?a-zA-Z$_) / idStartOther) identifierRest
def asIdentifier: Identifier = "as" !idPart
def moduleExportName: ModuleExportName = stringLiteral / identifierNameOrPrivate
def moduleExportNameStart = idStart / "#" / (?"')
def moduleSpecifier: Expression = stringLiteral / expression
// with { ... } or assert { ... } on the same line as the module specifier
def importAttributes: ImportAttributes = t:@(("with" / "assert") !idPart) -ws a:importAttributesBraces
    -> new ImportAttributes{Elements: $a, Token: text($t)}
def importAttributesBraces = "{" -ws es:importAttributeList? -ws "}"
    -> concat($es)
def importAttribute: ImportAttribute = n:(stringLiteral / identifierNameOrPrivate) -ws ":" -ws v:assignmentExpression
    -> new ImportAttribute{Name: $n, Value: $v}

// --- Exports ---
// export = x and export default x, in the await context
def exportAssignment: ExportAssignment = m:modifiers "export" !idPart -ws k:("=" !(?=>) / "default" !idPart) -ws
    [ctx = ctx - ctx / 2 % 2 * 2 + 2] e:assignmentExpression eos
    -> new ExportAssignment{Modifiers: $m, Expression: $e, IsExportEquals: text($k) == "="}
def namespaceExportDeclaration: NamespaceExportDeclaration = m:modifiers "export" !idPart -ws "as" !idPart -ws
    "namespace" !idPart -ws n:identifier eos -> new NamespaceExportDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n}
def exportDeclaration: ExportDeclaration = exportStarDeclaration / exportNamedDeclaration
def exportStarDeclaration: ExportDeclaration = m:modifiers "export" !idPart -ws (tt:"type" !idPart -ws)?
    (c:namespaceExport / "*") -ws "from" !idPart -ws [ctx = ctx - ctx / 2 % 2 * 2 + 2] s:moduleSpecifier
    (-sp at:importAttributes)? eos
    -> new ExportDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, ExportClause: $c, ModuleSpecifier: $s, Attributes: $at,
        IsTypeOnly: $tt != nil}
def exportNamedDeclaration: ExportDeclaration = m:modifiers "export" !idPart -ws (tt:"type" !idPart -ws)?
    c:namedExports (-ws "from" !idPart -ws [ctx = ctx - ctx / 2 % 2 * 2 + 2] s:moduleSpecifier
    (-sp at:importAttributes)?)? eos
    -> new ExportDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, ExportClause: $c, ModuleSpecifier: $s, Attributes: $at,
        IsTypeOnly: $tt != nil}
def namespaceExport: NamespaceExport = "*" -ws "as" !idPart -ws n:moduleExportName -> new NamespaceExport{Name: $n}
def namedExports: NamedExports = "{" -ws es:exportSpecifierList? -ws "}"
    -> new NamedExports{Elements: concat($es)}
def exportSpecifier: ExportSpecifier = exportSpecifierTypeAsAs / exportSpecifierTypeAsName / exportSpecifierTypeAs
    / exportSpecifierType / exportSpecifierPlain
def exportSpecifierTypeAsAs: ExportSpecifier = "type" !idPart -ws p:asIdentifier -ws "as" !idPart -ws
    n:moduleExportName -> new ExportSpecifier{PropertyName: $p, Name: $n, IsTypeOnly: true}
def exportSpecifierTypeAsName: ExportSpecifier = p:typeIdentifier -ws "as" !idPart -ws n:moduleExportName
    -> new ExportSpecifier{PropertyName: $p, Name: $n}
def exportSpecifierTypeAs: ExportSpecifier = "type" !idPart -ws n:asIdentifier !(-ws moduleExportNameStart)
    -> new ExportSpecifier{Name: $n, IsTypeOnly: true}
def exportSpecifierType: ExportSpecifier = "type" !idPart -ws &moduleExportNameStart
    (p:moduleExportName -ws "as" !idPart -ws n:moduleExportName / n:moduleExportName)
    -> new ExportSpecifier{PropertyName: $p, Name: $n, IsTypeOnly: true}
def exportSpecifierPlain: ExportSpecifier =
    (p:moduleExportName -ws "as" !idPart -ws n:moduleExportName / n:moduleExportName)
    -> new ExportSpecifier{PropertyName: $p, Name: $n}

// ===================================================================
// Modifiers and decorators (parseModifiers)
// ===================================================================

// Decorators, modifiers, and after modifiers more decorators and modifiers. Each modifier keyword is a
// modifier only before what can follow a modifier (nextTokenCanFollowModifier), so that public or
// declare stay names elsewhere; static is a modifier once.
def modifiers = (&"@" d1:decoratorList)? m1:modifierList? ([len($m1) > 0] d2:decoratorList m2:modifierList?)?
    -> concat($d1, $m1, $d2, $m2)
def decoratorList = ds:(d:decorator -ws)+ -> map($ds, (x) => $x.d)
def modifierList = b:(&(?acdeiopr) m:modifier -ws)* s:staticModifierList? a:(&(?acdeiopr) m:modifier -ws)*
    [len($b) > 0 || len($s) > 0]
    -> concat(map($b, (x) => $x.m), $s, map($a, (x) => $x.m))
def staticModifierList = &"s" m:staticModifier -ws -> list($m)
def modifier: Modifier = "export" !idPart &(-ws exportModifierFollows)
    / "default" !idPart &(-ws defaultModifierFollows)
    / "const" !idPart &(-ws "enum" !idPart)
    / ("abstract" / "accessor" / "async" / "declare" / "in" / "out" / "override" / "private" / "protected"
        / "public" / "readonly") !idPart &(sp canFollowModifier)
def staticModifier: Modifier = "static" !idPart &(-ws canFollowModifier)
def exportModifierFollows = "default" !idPart -ws defaultModifierFollows
    / "type" !idPart -ws canFollowExportModifier
    / !(("default" / "type") !idPart) canFollowExportModifier
def canFollowExportModifier = "@" / !((?*{) / "as" !idPart) canFollowModifier
def defaultModifierFollows = ("class" / "function" / "interface") !idPart / "@"
    / "abstract" !idPart sp "class" !idPart / "async" !idPart sp "function" !idPart
def canFollowModifier = (?[{*) / "..." / literalPropertyNameStart
def literalPropertyNameStart = idStart / "#" / (?"'0-9) / "." (?0-9)

// Class members also take const as a modifier, and static before "{" starts a static block.
def classModifiers = (&"@" d1:decoratorList)? m1:classModifierList? ([len($m1) > 0] d2:decoratorList m2:classModifierList?)?
    -> concat($d1, $m1, $d2, $m2)
def classModifierList = b:(&(?acdeiopr) m:classModifier -ws)* s:classStaticModifierList?
    a:(&(?acdeiopr) m:classModifier -ws)* [len($b) > 0 || len($s) > 0] -> concat(map($b, (x) => $x.m), $s, map($a, (x) => $x.m))
def classStaticModifierList = &"s" m:classStaticModifier -ws -> list($m)
def classModifier: Modifier = "const" !idPart &(sp canFollowModifier) / modifier
def classStaticModifier: Modifier = "static" !idPart !(-ws "{") &(-ws canFollowModifier)

// Type members take no decorators; type parameters take const, in and out.
def typeMemberModifiers = ms:modifierList? -> concat($ms)
def typeParameterModifiers = b:(&(?acdeiopr) m:classModifier -ws)* s:staticModifierList?
    a:(&(?acdeiopr) m:classModifier -ws)*
    -> concat(map($b, (x) => $x.m), $s, map($a, (x) => $x.m))

// A decorator is a left-hand side expression in the decorator context, where "[" is not an element access.
def decorator: Decorator = "@" -ws [ctx = ctx - ctx / 8 % 2 * 8 + 8] e:leftHandSideExpression
    -> new Decorator{Expression: $e}

// ===================================================================
// Expressions
// ===================================================================

// parseExpression: a comma expression, outside the decorator context
def expression: Expression = [ctx = ctx - ctx / 8 % 4 * 8] e:commaExpression -> $e
// allowInAnd(parseExpression)
def expressionAllowIn: Expression = [ctx = ctx - ctx / 4 % 8 * 4] e:commaExpression -> $e
def commaExpression: Expression = first:assignmentExpressionInner rest:(-ws o:commaToken -ws e:assignmentExpressionInner)*
    -> foldl($first, $rest, (acc, r) => new BinaryExpression{Left: $acc, OperatorToken: $r.o, Right: $r.e})
// parseAssignmentExpressionOrHigher(allowReturnTypeInArrowFunction = true)
def assignmentExpression: Expression = [ctx = ctx - ctx / 8 % 4 * 8] e:assignmentExpressionInner -> $e
def assignmentExpressionAllowIn: Expression = [ctx = ctx - ctx / 4 % 8 * 4] e:assignmentExpressionInner -> $e

// parseAssignmentExpressionOrHigher: a yield expression, an arrow function, an assignment to a left-hand
// side expression, or a conditional expression.
def assignmentExpressionInner: Expression = (&"yield" e:yieldExpression / &("async" !idPart / (?(<)) e:arrowFunction
    / &"async" e:asyncSimpleArrowFunction / &((?a-zA-Z$_\\\u{80}-\u{10FFFF}) identifierRest -ws "=>") e:simpleArrowFunction / e:assignment
    / e:conditionalOrBinaryExpression) -> $e

// yield is an expression in the yield context, or before an identifier, keyword or literal on the
// same line; its operand must be on the same line.
def yieldExpression: YieldExpression = "yield" !idPart ([ctx % 2 == 1] / &(sp identifierOrKeywordOrLiteralStart))
    (-sp !nlStart (at:asteriskToken -ws)? e:assignmentExpression)?
    -> new YieldExpression{AsteriskToken: $at, Expression: $e}
def identifierOrKeywordOrLiteralStart = idStart / "#" / (?0-9"') / "." (?0-9)
def nlStart = (?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}) / "/*"

def assignment: BinaryExpression = l:leftHandSideExpression -ws &(?>*<&|?+\-/%^=) o:assignmentOperator -ws r:assignmentExpressionInner
    -> new BinaryExpression{Left: $l, OperatorToken: $o, Right: $r}
def assignmentOperator: Token = ">>>=" / "**=" / "<<=" / ">>=" / "&&=" / "||=" / "??=" / "+=" / "-=" / "*=" / "/="
    / "%=" / "&=" / "|=" / "^=" / "=" !(?=>)

// The true branch allows `in` and arrow functions without a return type (allowReturnTypeInArrowFunction
// = false), and is outside the decorator context.
def conditionalOrBinaryExpression: Expression = c:binaryExpression
    rest:(-ws q:conditionalQuestionToken -ws t:conditionalWhenTrue -ws k:colonToken -ws
        f:conditionalWhenFalse)*
    -> foldl($c, $rest, (acc, r) => new ConditionalExpression{Condition: $acc, QuestionToken: $r.q, WhenTrue: $r.t,
        ColonToken: $r.k, WhenFalse: $r.f})
def conditionalWhenTrue: Expression = [ctx = ctx - ctx / 4 % 8 * 4 + 16] e:assignmentExpressionInner -> $e
def conditionalWhenFalse: Expression = e:assignmentExpressionInner -> $e
def conditionalQuestionToken: Token = "?" !"?" !("." !(?0-9))

// --- Arrow functions (tryParseParenthesizedArrowFunctionExpression, isParenthesizedArrowFunctionExpression) ---
// In a .tsx file, <T> starts JSX; a generic arrow function needs <T,>, <T = ...> or <T extends ...>.
def arrowFunction: ArrowFunction = ml:arrowAsyncModifier? !arrowParenthesisIsNotParameterList
    [ctx = ctx - ctx % 4 + len($ml) * 2] (t:arrowTypeParameters -ws)? &"(" ps:parameterList rt:returnType? -ws
    a:equalsGreaterThanToken -ws b:arrowBody ([ctx / 16 % 2 == 0] / [$rt == nil] / &(-ws ":"))
    -> new ArrowFunction{Modifiers: concat($ml), TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps, Type: $rt,
        EqualsGreaterThanToken: $a, Body: $b}
def arrowAsyncModifier = m:asyncKeywordModifier -sp &(?(<) -> list($m)
def asyncKeywordModifier: Modifier = "async" !idPart
def arrowTypeParameters = &("<" -ws ("const" !idPart / identifier)) ([ctx < 64] / &tsxArrowTypeParametersStart)
    tp:typeParameters -> $tp
def tsxArrowTypeParametersStart = "<" -ws ("const" !idPart -ws)? identifier -ws
    ("extends" !idPart -ws !(?=>/) / (?,=))
// (yield) and (await) are not parameter lists where yield and await are not identifiers.
def arrowParenthesisIsNotParameterList = "(" -ws ("yield" !idPart [ctx % 2 == 1] / "await" !idPart [ctx / 2 % 2 == 1]
    / !(!("async" !idPart) modifierKeyword -ws identifier) (identifier / "this" !idPart) -ws !(?:?,=\)))
// x => ..., with the parameter an identifier in the current context
def simpleArrowFunction: ArrowFunction = p:simpleArrowParameter -ws a:equalsGreaterThanToken -ws [ctx = ctx - ctx % 4]
    b:arrowBody -> new ArrowFunction{Parameters: list($p), EqualsGreaterThanToken: $a, Body: $b}
def simpleArrowParameter: Parameter = n:identifier -> new Parameter{Name: $n}
// async x => ..., all on one line
def asyncSimpleArrowFunction: ArrowFunction = m:asyncKeywordModifier -sp !(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}) p:simpleArrowParameter -sp
    a:equalsGreaterThanToken -ws [ctx = ctx - ctx % 4 + 2] b:arrowBody
    -> new ArrowFunction{Modifiers: list($m), Parameters: list($p), EqualsGreaterThanToken: $a, Body: $b}
def arrowBody: ConciseBody = block / assignmentExpressionInner

// --- Binary expressions (parseBinaryExpressionRest) ---
// The levels are those of getBinaryOperatorPrecedence; as and satisfies take a type on the same line.
// skip is sp and each operator skips the whitespace before it, so that `as` can require no line break.
// Every operator is tried after every operand, so each starts with a silent test of the character where it can
// start (&(?...): a line break or "/" for the whitespace and comments before it, or a character of the operator),
// which fails without a rule call or an expectation. For the same reason skip, which the Pratt loop runs before
// each operator and operand, is sp behind a silent test of whether it has anything to skip (here and in the other
// Pratt expressions).
def binaryExpression: Expression = pratt {
    skip (&(? \t\v\f\u{A0}\u0085\u{1680}\u{2000}-\u{200B}\u{202F}\u{205F}\u{3000}\u{FEFF}/) sp)
    operand unaryExpression
    level {
        infix left &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/?|) -ws o:coalesceOrToken -- -ws
            -> new BinaryExpression{Left: $lhs, OperatorToken: $o, Right: $rhs}
    }
    level {
        infix left &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/&) -ws o:ampersandAmpersandToken -- -ws
            -> new BinaryExpression{Left: $lhs, OperatorToken: $o, Right: $rhs}
    }
    level {
        infix left &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/|) -ws o:barToken -- -ws
            -> new BinaryExpression{Left: $lhs, OperatorToken: $o, Right: $rhs}
    }
    level {
        infix left &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/^) -ws o:caretToken -- -ws
            -> new BinaryExpression{Left: $lhs, OperatorToken: $o, Right: $rhs}
    }
    level {
        infix left &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/&) -ws o:ampersandToken -- -ws
            -> new BinaryExpression{Left: $lhs, OperatorToken: $o, Right: $rhs}
    }
    level {
        infix left &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/=!) -ws o:equalityToken -- -ws
            -> new BinaryExpression{Left: $lhs, OperatorToken: $o, Right: $rhs}
    }
    level {
        infix left &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/<>i) -ws o:relationalToken -- -ws
            -> new BinaryExpression{Left: $lhs, OperatorToken: $o, Right: $rhs}
        postfix &(?a) "as" !idPart -- -ws t:typeNode -> new AsExpression{Expression: $lhs, Type: $t}
        postfix &(?s) "satisfies" !idPart -- -ws t:typeNode -> new SatisfiesExpression{Expression: $lhs, Type: $t}
    }
    level {
        infix left &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/<>) -ws o:shiftToken -- -ws
            -> new BinaryExpression{Left: $lhs, OperatorToken: $o, Right: $rhs}
    }
    level {
        infix left &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/+-) -ws o:additiveToken -- -ws
            -> new BinaryExpression{Left: $lhs, OperatorToken: $o, Right: $rhs}
    }
    level {
        infix left &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/*%) -ws o:multiplicativeToken -- -ws
            -> new BinaryExpression{Left: $lhs, OperatorToken: $o, Right: $rhs}
    }
    level {
        infix right &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/*) -ws o:asteriskAsteriskToken -- -ws
            -> new BinaryExpression{Left: $lhs, OperatorToken: $o, Right: $rhs}
    }
}
// Operator tokens, each not the start of a longer token (maximal munch).
def coalesceOrToken: Token = "??" !"=" / "||" !"="
def ampersandAmpersandToken: Token = "&&" !"="
def barToken: Token = "|" !(?|=)
def caretToken: Token = "^" !"="
def ampersandToken: Token = "&" !(?&=)
def equalityToken: Token = "===" / "!==" / "==" / "!="
// In a .tsx file, </ is the start of a closing tag.
def relationalToken: Token = "<=" / ">=" / "<" !(?<=) !([ctx >= 64] "/" !"*") / ">" !(?>=)
    / "instanceof" !idPart / [ctx / 4 % 2 == 0] "in" !idPart
def shiftToken: Token = ">>>" !"=" / ">>" !(?>=) / "<<" !"="
def additiveToken: Token = "+" !(?+=) / "-" !(?\-=)
def multiplicativeToken: Token = "*" !(?*=) / "/" !"=" / "%" !"="
def asteriskAsteriskToken: Token = "**" !"="
// isBinaryOperator
def binaryOperatorStart = coalesceOrToken / ampersandAmpersandToken / barToken / caretToken / ampersandToken
    / equalityToken / relationalToken / shiftToken / additiveToken / multiplicativeToken / asteriskAsteriskToken
    / ("as" / "satisfies") !idPart

// --- Unary expressions (parseUnaryExpressionOrHigher) ---
// A unary operator other than ++ and -- may not be the left operand of **.
def unaryExpression: Expression = (&(?+\-~!<dtva) &unaryOperatorStart u:simpleUnaryExpression !(-ws "**" !"=")
    / !(&(?+\-~!<dtva) unaryOperatorStart) u:updateExpression) -> $u
def unaryOperatorStart = &(?+\-~!<dtva)
    ("+" !"+" / "-" !"-" / (?~!) / ("delete" / "typeof" / "void" / "await") !idPart / [ctx < 64] "<")
def simpleUnaryExpression: Expression = prefixUnaryExpression / deleteExpression / typeOfExpression / voidExpression
    / typeAssertion / jsxUnaryExpression / awaitExpression / updateExpression
def prefixUnaryExpression: PrefixUnaryExpression = o:@("+" !"+" / "-" !"-" / "~" / "!") -ws e:simpleUnaryExpression
    -> new PrefixUnaryExpression{Operator: text($o), Operand: $e}
def deleteExpression: DeleteExpression = "delete" !idPart -ws e:simpleUnaryExpression -> new DeleteExpression{Expression: $e}
def typeOfExpression: TypeOfExpression = "typeof" !idPart -ws e:simpleUnaryExpression -> new TypeOfExpression{Expression: $e}
def voidExpression: VoidExpression = "void" !idPart -ws e:simpleUnaryExpression -> new VoidExpression{Expression: $e}
// await is an expression in the await context, or before an identifier, keyword or literal on the same line.
def awaitExpression: AwaitExpression = "await" !idPart ([ctx / 2 % 2 == 1] / &(sp identifierOrKeywordOrLiteralStart))
    -ws e:simpleUnaryExpression -> new AwaitExpression{Expression: $e}
// <T>x, only in a .ts file
def typeAssertion: TypeAssertionExpression = [ctx < 64] "<" !(?<=) -ws t:typeNode -ws ">" -ws e:simpleUnaryExpression
    -> new TypeAssertionExpression{Type: $t, Expression: $e}
def jsxUnaryExpression: Expression = [ctx >= 64] &"<" e:jsxElementOrFragment -> $e

// parseUpdateExpression
def updateExpression: Expression = (&(?+\-) e:prefixUpdateExpression / [ctx >= 64] &"<" e:jsxPrimaryExpression
    / e:postfixOrLeftHandSideExpression) -> $e
// A left-hand side expression, parsed once, and one ++ or -- after it on the same line.
def postfixOrLeftHandSideExpression: Expression = e:leftHandSideExpression rest:(-sp o:@("++" / "--"))*
    [len($rest) <= 1]
    -> foldl($e, $rest, (acc, r) => new PostfixUnaryExpression{Operand: $acc, Operator: text($r.o)})
def prefixUpdateExpression: PrefixUnaryExpression = o:@("++" / "--") -ws e:leftHandSideExpression
    -> new PrefixUnaryExpression{Operator: text($o), Operand: $e}
// JSX in an expression, which may not be followed by "<" ("JSX expressions must have one parent element").
def jsxPrimaryExpression: Expression = [ctx >= 64] &("<" -ws (idStart / ">")) e:jsxElementOrFragment
    !(-ws "<" !(?<=)) -> $e

// --- Left-hand side expressions (parseLeftHandSideExpressionOrHigher, parseMemberExpressionRest,
// parseCallExpressionRest) ---
// Type arguments in an expression are taken only before what can follow them
// (canFollowTypeArgumentsInExpression); otherwise < is a comparison.
// As in binaryExpression, each postfix operator starts with a silent test of its first character (or of a line
// break or "/" before it), and the operand that is almost always the one, primaryExpression, comes first.
def leftHandSideExpression: Expression = pratt {
    skip (&(? \t\v\f\u{A0}\u0085\u{1680}\u{2000}-\u{200B}\u{202F}\u{205F}\u{3000}\u{FEFF}/) sp)
    operand primaryExpression
    operand superExpression
    operand importCallee
    operand importMetaProperty
    level {
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/.) -ws "." !(?0-9.) -- -ws n:memberName
            -> new PropertyAccessExpression{Expression: $lhs, Name: $n}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/?) -ws q:questionDotToken -- -ws n:identifierName
            -> new PropertyAccessExpression{Expression: $lhs, QuestionDotToken: $q, Name: $n}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/[) -ws [ctx / 8 % 2 == 0] "[" -- -ws e:expressionAllowIn -ws "]"
            -> new ElementAccessExpression{Expression: $lhs, ArgumentExpression: $e}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/?) -ws q:questionDotToken -- -ws "[" -ws e:expressionAllowIn -ws "]"
            -> new ElementAccessExpression{Expression: $lhs, QuestionDotToken: $q, ArgumentExpression: $e}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/<`) -ws (t:typeArgumentsInExpression -ws)? &"`" -- l:taggedTemplate
            -> new TaggedTemplateExpression{Tag: $lhs, TypeArguments: concat($t), Template: $l}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/?) -ws q:questionDotToken -- -ws (t:typeArgumentsInExpression -ws)? l:taggedTemplate
            -> new TaggedTemplateExpression{Tag: $lhs, QuestionDotToken: $q, TypeArguments: concat($t), Template: $l}
        postfix &(?!) "!" !"=" -> new NonNullExpression{Expression: $lhs}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/<) -ws t:typeArgumentsInExpression
            -> new ExpressionWithTypeArguments{Expression: $lhs, TypeArguments: $t}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/<() -ws (t:typeArgumentsInExpression -ws)? &"(" -- a:arguments
            -> new CallExpression{Expression: $lhs, TypeArguments: concat($t), Arguments: $a}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/?) -ws q:questionDotToken -- -ws (t:typeArgumentsInExpression -ws)? a:arguments
            -> new CallExpression{Expression: $lhs, QuestionDotToken: $q, TypeArguments: concat($t), Arguments: $a}
    }
}
// The same without instantiation expressions, for heritage clauses, which take type arguments of their own.
def heritageExpression: Expression = pratt {
    skip (&(? \t\v\f\u{A0}\u0085\u{1680}\u{2000}-\u{200B}\u{202F}\u{205F}\u{3000}\u{FEFF}/) sp)
    operand primaryExpression
    operand superExpression
    operand importCallee
    operand importMetaProperty
    level {
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/.) -ws "." !(?0-9.) -- -ws n:memberName
            -> new PropertyAccessExpression{Expression: $lhs, Name: $n}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/?) -ws q:questionDotToken -- -ws n:identifierName
            -> new PropertyAccessExpression{Expression: $lhs, QuestionDotToken: $q, Name: $n}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/[) -ws [ctx / 8 % 2 == 0] "[" -- -ws e:expressionAllowIn -ws "]"
            -> new ElementAccessExpression{Expression: $lhs, ArgumentExpression: $e}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/?) -ws q:questionDotToken -- -ws "[" -ws e:expressionAllowIn -ws "]"
            -> new ElementAccessExpression{Expression: $lhs, QuestionDotToken: $q, ArgumentExpression: $e}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/<`) -ws (t:typeArgumentsInExpression -ws)? &"`" -- l:taggedTemplate
            -> new TaggedTemplateExpression{Tag: $lhs, TypeArguments: concat($t), Template: $l}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/?) -ws q:questionDotToken -- -ws (t:typeArgumentsInExpression -ws)? l:taggedTemplate
            -> new TaggedTemplateExpression{Tag: $lhs, QuestionDotToken: $q, TypeArguments: concat($t), Template: $l}
        postfix &(?!) "!" !"=" -> new NonNullExpression{Expression: $lhs}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/<() -ws (t:typeArgumentsInExpression -ws)? &"(" -- a:arguments
            -> new CallExpression{Expression: $lhs, TypeArguments: concat($t), Arguments: $a}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/?) -ws q:questionDotToken -- -ws (t:typeArgumentsInExpression -ws)? a:arguments
            -> new CallExpression{Expression: $lhs, QuestionDotToken: $q, TypeArguments: concat($t), Arguments: $a}
    }
}
// The target of new: member accesses, element accesses, tagged templates and non-null assertions, without
// calls or optional chains (parseMemberExpressionRest with allowOptionalChain = false).
def newTarget: Expression = pratt {
    skip (&(? \t\v\f\u{A0}\u0085\u{1680}\u{2000}-\u{200B}\u{202F}\u{205F}\u{3000}\u{FEFF}/) sp)
    operand primaryExpression
    operand superKeyword
    level {
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/.) -ws "." !(?0-9.) -- -ws n:memberName
            -> new PropertyAccessExpression{Expression: $lhs, Name: $n}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/[) -ws [ctx / 8 % 2 == 0] "[" -- -ws e:expressionAllowIn -ws "]"
            -> new ElementAccessExpression{Expression: $lhs, ArgumentExpression: $e}
        postfix &(?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}/<`) -ws (t:typeArgumentsInExpression -ws)? &"`" -- l:taggedTemplate
            -> new TaggedTemplateExpression{Tag: $lhs, TypeArguments: concat($t), Template: $l}
        postfix &(?!) "!" !"=" -> new NonNullExpression{Expression: $lhs}
    }
}
def memberName: MemberName = privateIdentifier / identifierName
def questionDotToken: Token = "?." !(?0-9)

// parseTypeArgumentsInExpression: "<" types ">" not followed by ">" or "=", then what can follow type
// arguments: "(" or a template; else not "<", ">", "+" or "-", and a line break, a binary operator or
// something that cannot start an expression. An instantiation expression may not be followed by a
// property access, so "." and "?." before a name are excluded too.
def typeArgumentsInExpression = "<" -ws [ctx = ctx - ctx % 4] ts:typeList? -ws ">" !(?>=) &typeArgumentsCanFollow
    -> concat($ts)
def typeArgumentsCanFollow = -ws (?(`)
    / !(-ws ("<" !(?<=) / ">" / "+" !(?+=) / "-" !(?\-=) / "." !(?0-9) / "?." !(?0-9) -ws idStart))
        (nlAhead / -ws binaryOperatorStart / !(-ws expressionStart))
// isStartOfExpression
def expressionStart = (?0-9"'`([{/~!#@) / "<" !(?<=) / "+" !"=" / "-" !"=" / "." (?0-9)
    / ("this" / "super" / "null" / "true" / "false" / "function" / "class" / "new" / "delete" / "typeof" / "void")
        !idPart
    / "import" !idPart -ws (?(<.)
    / !reservedWord idStart
    / binaryOperatorStart

def arguments = "(" -ws [ctx = ctx - ctx / 4 % 8 * 4] as:argumentList? -ws ")" -> concat($as)
def argumentList = first:argument rest:(-ws "," -ws a:argument)* (-ws ",")?
    -> concat(list($first), map($rest, (r) => $r.a))
def argument: Expression = spreadElement / assignmentExpressionInner
def spreadElement: SpreadElement = "..." -ws e:assignmentExpression -> new SpreadElement{Expression: $e}

// super must be followed by "(", "." or "["
def superExpression: SuperExpression = "super" !idPart &(-ws (?(.[))
def superKeyword: SuperExpression = "super" !idPart
def importCallee: ImportExpression = "import" !idPart &(-ws (?(<))
def importMetaProperty: MetaProperty = "import" !idPart -ws "." -ws n:identifierNameOrPrivate
    -> new MetaProperty{KeywordToken: "import", Name: $n}

// --- Primary expressions (parsePrimaryExpression) ---
// An identifier is the most common primary expression, and it cannot be mistaken for a keyword (async function is
// a function expression). The first character tells words from the rest; (?a-zA-Z$_\\\u{80}-\u{10FFFF})
// is the start of an identifier, or a character that may turn out not to be.
def primaryExpression: Expression = (&(?a-zA-Z$_\\\u{80}-\u{10FFFF}) e:wordPrimary / e:symbolPrimary)
    #error(message="expected an expression") -> $e
def wordPrimary: Expression = (!("async" !idPart -sp "function" !idPart) e:identifier / e:thisKeyword / e:nullKeyword
    / e:booleanKeyword / e:functionExpression / e:classExpressionPrimary / e:newExpression) -> $e
def symbolPrimary: Expression = stringLiteral / numericOrBigIntLiteral / noSubstitutionTemplateLiteral
    / templateExpression / parenthesizedExpression / arrayLiteralExpression / objectLiteralExpression
    / classExpressionPrimary / regularExpressionLiteral / privateIdentifier
def numericOrBigIntLiteral: Expression = &(?0-9.) e:(numericLiteral / bigIntLiteral) -> $e
def thisKeyword: ThisExpression = "this" !idPart
def nullKeyword: NullLiteral = "null" !idPart
def booleanKeyword: BooleanLiteral = ("true" / "false") !idPart
def parenthesizedExpression: ParenthesizedExpression = "(" -ws e:expressionAllowIn -ws ")"
    -> new ParenthesizedExpression{Expression: $e}
// An element is a spread, an expression or an omitted expression (a hole).
def arrayLiteralExpression: ArrayLiteralExpression = "[" -ws [ctx = ctx - ctx / 8 % 4 * 8]
    es:arrayElementList? -ws "]"
    -> new ArrayLiteralExpression{Elements: concat($es)}
def arrayElement: Expression = spreadElement / assignmentExpressionInner / omittedExpression
def objectLiteralExpression: ObjectLiteralExpression = "{" -ws
    ps:objectLiteralElementList? -ws "}"
    -> new ObjectLiteralExpression{Properties: concat($ps)}
// parseObjectLiteralElement
def objectLiteralElement: ObjectLiteralElement = spreadAssignment / objectAccessor / objectMemberNotAccessor
def objectAccessor: ObjectLiteralElement = &(modifiers accessorKeyword) m:(objectGetAccessor / objectSetAccessor) -> $m
def objectMemberNotAccessor: ObjectLiteralElement = !(modifiers accessorKeyword)
    m:(objectMethod / shorthandPropertyAssignment / propertyAssignment) -> $m
def objectLiteralElementStart = (?[*.) / literalPropertyNameStart
def spreadAssignment: SpreadAssignment = "..." -ws e:assignmentExpression -> new SpreadAssignment{Expression: $e}
def objectGetAccessor: GetAccessor = m:modifiers "get" !idPart &(-ws canFollowGetOrSet) -ws n:propertyName
    [ctx = ctx - ctx % 32] (-ws t:typeParameters)? -ws ps:parameterList rt:returnType? (-ws fb:block / !(-ws "{") eos)
    -> new GetAccessor{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps, Type: $rt, Body: $fb}
def objectSetAccessor: SetAccessor = m:modifiers "set" !idPart &(-ws canFollowGetOrSet) -ws n:propertyName
    [ctx = ctx - ctx % 32] (-ws t:typeParameters)? -ws ps:parameterList rt:returnType? (-ws fb:block / !(-ws "{") eos)
    -> new SetAccessor{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps, Type: $rt, Body: $fb}
def objectMethod: MethodDeclaration = (&(am:asyncModifierScan))? m:modifiers (s:asteriskToken -ws)? n:propertyName
    (-ws qt:questionToken)? (-ws xt:exclamationToken)? ([$s != nil] / &(-ws (?(<)))
    [ctx = ctx - ctx % 32 + len($s) + len($am) / 5 * 2]
    (-ws t:typeParameters)? -ws ps:parameterList rt:returnType? (-ws fb:block / !(-ws "{") eos)
    -> new MethodDeclaration{Modifiers: $m, AsteriskToken: $s, Name: $n, QuestionToken: $qt, ExclamationToken: $xt,
        TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps, Type: $rt, Body: $fb}
// An identifier not followed by ":" is a shorthand property, with an optional = initializer.
def shorthandPropertyAssignment: ShorthandPropertyAssignment = m:modifiers n:identifier (-ws qt:questionToken)?
    (-ws xt:exclamationToken)? !(-ws ":") (-ws eq:equalsToken -ws [ctx = ctx - ctx / 4 % 2 * 4] v:assignmentExpression)?
    -> new ShorthandPropertyAssignment{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, QuestionToken: $qt, ExclamationToken: $xt,
        EqualsToken: $eq, ObjectAssignmentInitializer: $v}
def propertyAssignment: PropertyAssignment = m:modifiers n:propertyName (-ws qt:questionToken)?
    (-ws xt:exclamationToken)? -ws ":" -ws [ctx = ctx - ctx / 4 % 2 * 4] v:assignmentExpression
    -> new PropertyAssignment{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, QuestionToken: $qt, ExclamationToken: $xt, Initializer: $v}

def functionExpression: FunctionExpression = ml:asyncFunctionModifier? "function" !idPart (-ws s:asteriskToken)?
    [ctx = ctx - ctx % 32 + len($s) + len($ml) * 2] (-ws i:bindingIdentifier)? (-ws t:typeParameters)? -ws
    ps:parameterList rt:returnType? -ws b:block
    -> new FunctionExpression{Modifiers: concat($ml), AsteriskToken: $s, Name: $i, TypeParameters: concat($t),
        Parameters: $ps, Type: $rt, Body: $b}
def asyncFunctionModifier = m:asyncKeywordModifier -sp &("function" !idPart) -> list($m)
// class ... or decorators and class (parseDecoratedExpression)
def classExpressionPrimary: ClassExpression = &("class" !idPart / "@") c:classExpression -> $c

// new.target, or new and a member expression with optional type arguments and arguments
// (parseNewExpressionOrNewDotTarget); new x?.y is an error.
def newExpression: Expression = newTargetMetaProperty / newExpressionWithTarget
def newTargetMetaProperty: MetaProperty = "new" !idPart -ws "." -ws n:identifierNameOrPrivate
    -> new MetaProperty{KeywordToken: "new", Name: $n}
def newExpressionWithTarget: NewExpression = "new" !idPart -ws e:newTarget (-ws t:typeArgumentsInExpression)?
    !(-ws "?." !(?0-9)) (-ws as:arguments)?
    -> new NewExpression{Expression: $e, TypeArguments: concat($t), Arguments: $as}

// --- Templates ---
// An untagged template must have valid escape sequences; a tagged one may have any.
def templateExpression: TemplateExpression = h:templateHead ss:templateSpans
    -> new TemplateExpression{Head: $h, TemplateSpans: $ss}
def templateSpans = ms:(-ws m:templateSpanMiddle)* -ws t:templateSpanTail -> concat(map($ms, (x) => $x.m), list($t))
def templateSpanMiddle: TemplateSpan = e:expressionAllowIn -ws l:templateMiddle -> new TemplateSpan{Expression: $e, Literal: $l}
def templateSpanTail: TemplateSpan = e:expressionAllowIn -ws l:templateTail -> new TemplateSpan{Expression: $e, Literal: $l}
def taggedTemplate: TemplateLiteral = rawNoSubstitutionTemplateLiteral / rawTemplateExpression
def rawTemplateExpression: TemplateExpression = h:rawTemplateHead ss:rawTemplateSpans
    -> new TemplateExpression{Head: $h, TemplateSpans: $ss}
def rawTemplateSpans = ms:(-ws m:rawTemplateSpanMiddle)* -ws t:rawTemplateSpanTail -> concat(map($ms, (x) => $x.m), list($t))
def rawTemplateSpanMiddle: TemplateSpan = e:expressionAllowIn -ws l:rawTemplateMiddle
    -> new TemplateSpan{Expression: $e, Literal: $l}
def rawTemplateSpanTail: TemplateSpan = e:expressionAllowIn -ws l:rawTemplateTail
    -> new TemplateSpan{Expression: $e, Literal: $l}

// ===================================================================
// JSX (parseJsxElementOrSelfClosingElementOrFragment)
// ===================================================================

def jsxElementOrFragment: Expression = jsxSelfClosingElement / jsxElement / jsxFragment
def jsxSelfClosingElement: JsxSelfClosingElement = "<" -ws n:jsxElementName (-ws t:typeArguments)? -ws
    a:jsxAttributes -ws "/" -ws ">"
    -> new JsxSelfClosingElement{TagName: $n, TypeArguments: concat($t), Attributes: $a}
// The closing tag must name the opening tag.
def jsxElement: JsxElement = &("<" -ws on:jsxElementName) o:jsxOpeningElement cs:jsxChild*
    &("</" -ws cn:jsxElementName) c:jsxClosingElement [text($on) == text($cn)]
    -> new JsxElement{OpeningElement: $o, Children: $cs, ClosingElement: $c}
def jsxOpeningElement: JsxOpeningElement = "<" -ws n:jsxElementName (-ws t:typeArguments)? -ws a:jsxAttributes
    -ws ">" -> new JsxOpeningElement{TagName: $n, TypeArguments: concat($t), Attributes: $a}
def jsxClosingElement: JsxClosingElement = "</" -ws n:jsxElementName -ws ">" -> new JsxClosingElement{TagName: $n}
def jsxFragment: JsxFragment = o:jsxOpeningFragment cs:jsxChild* c:jsxClosingFragment
    -> new JsxFragment{OpeningFragment: $o, Children: $cs, ClosingFragment: $c}
def jsxOpeningFragment: JsxOpeningFragment = "<" -ws ">"
def jsxClosingFragment: JsxClosingFragment = "</" -ws ">"

// A tag name: an identifier with dashes, a namespaced name, this, or a member access.
def jsxElementName: JsxTagName = jsxNamespacedName / jsxMemberName
def jsxMemberName: JsxTagName = first:jsxTagNameStart rest:(-ws "." -ws n:identifierName)*
    -> foldl($first, $rest, (acc, r) => new PropertyAccessExpression{Expression: $acc, Name: $r.n})
def jsxTagNameStart: JsxTagNameStart = jsxThis / jsxIdentifier
def jsxThis: ThisExpression = "this" !(idPart / "-")
def jsxIdentifier: Identifier = "#"? idStart (idPart / "-")*
def jsxNamespacedName: JsxNamespacedName = s:jsxIdentifier -ws ":" -ws n:jsxIdentifier
    -> new JsxNamespacedName{Namespace: $s, Name: $n}

def jsxAttributes: JsxAttributes = ps:jsxAttributeLikeList?
    -> new JsxAttributes{Properties: concat($ps)}
def jsxAttributeLike: JsxAttributeLike = jsxSpreadAttribute / jsxAttribute
def jsxAttribute: JsxAttribute = n:jsxAttributeName (-ws "=" -ws i:jsxAttributeValue)?
    -> new JsxAttribute{Name: $n, Initializer: $i}
def jsxAttributeName: JsxAttributeName = jsxNamespacedName / jsxIdentifier
def jsxAttributeValue: JsxAttributeValue = jsxAttributeString / jsxAttributeExpression / jsxElementOrFragmentValue
def jsxElementOrFragmentValue: JsxAttributeValue = jsxSelfClosingElement / jsxElement / jsxFragment
def jsxAttributeString: StringLiteral = "\"" (?^")* "\"" / "'" (?^')* "'"
def jsxAttributeExpression: JsxExpression = "{" -ws e:expression? -ws "}" -> new JsxExpression{Expression: $e}
def jsxSpreadAttribute: JsxSpreadAttribute = "{" -ws "..." -ws e:expression -ws "}"
    -> new JsxSpreadAttribute{Expression: $e}

// Children: text (where ">" and "}" are errors), {expressions} and elements.
def jsxChild: JsxChild = jsxText / jsxChildExpression / jsxChildElement
def jsxText: JsxText = (?^{}<>)+
def jsxChildExpression: JsxExpression = "{" -ws (dt:dotDotDotToken -ws)? e:expression? -ws "}"
    -> new JsxExpression{DotDotDotToken: $dt, Expression: $e}
def jsxChildElement: JsxChild = !"</" e:(jsxSelfClosingElement / jsxElement / jsxFragment) -> $e

// ===================================================================
// Types (parseType)
// ===================================================================

// Types are parsed outside the yield and await contexts.
def typeNode: TypeNode = [ctx = ctx - ctx % 4] t:typeInner -> $t
def typeInner: TypeNode = functionType / constructorType / conditionalOrHigher
// The extends type of a conditional type and the constraint of infer disallow conditional types.
def typeNoConditional: TypeNode = [ctx = ctx - ctx / 32 % 2 * 32 + 32] t:typeInner -> $t
def typeAllowConditional: TypeNode = [ctx = ctx - ctx / 32 % 2 * 32] t:typeInner -> $t
// A union or intersection type, parsed once, and the conditional type it may check (extends ... ? ... : ...).
def conditionalOrHigher: TypeNode = c:unionOrHigher
    rest:([ctx / 32 % 2 == 0] -sp "extends" !idPart -ws e:typeNoConditional -ws "?" -ws t:typeAllowConditional -ws ":"
        -ws f:typeAllowConditional)*
    -> foldl($c, $rest, (acc, r) => new ConditionalType{CheckType: $acc, ExtendsType: $r.e, TrueType: $r.t,
        FalseType: $r.f})
def typeOrTypePredicate: TypeNode = typePredicate / typeNode
def typePredicate: TypePredicate = n:identifier -sp "is" !idPart -ws t:typeNode
    -> new TypePredicate{ParameterName: $n, Type: $t}

def functionType: FunctionType = &(?(<) (&"<" / &unambiguousFunctionTypeStart) (t:typeParameters -ws)? ps:parameterList
    -ws "=>" -ws r:returnTypeOfType
    -> new FunctionType{TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps, Type: $r}
def constructorType: ConstructorType = &(("abstract" / "new") !idPart) (am:abstractModifier -ws)? "new" !idPart -ws (t:typeParameters -ws)?
    ps:parameterList -ws "=>" -ws r:returnTypeOfType
    -> new ConstructorType{Modifiers: concat($am), TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps, Type: $r}
def abstractModifier = m:abstractKeywordModifier -> list($m)
def abstractKeywordModifier: Modifier = "abstract" !idPart
def returnTypeOfType: TypeNode = [ctx = ctx - ctx / 32 % 2 * 32] t:typeOrTypePredicate -> $t

// A leading | or & makes a union or intersection of one type.
// A | or & after a type is always followed by a type: a failed one is an error, not the end of the type.
def unionOrHigher: TypeNode = (u:leadingUnionType / u:plainOrUnionType) -> $u
def leadingUnionType: UnionType = barToken -ws f:intersectionOrHigher r:(-ws barToken -ws t:intersectionOrHigher)*
    !(-ws barToken) -> new UnionType{Types: concat(list($f), map($r, (x) => $x.t))}
def plainOrUnionType: TypeNode = f:intersectionOrHigher
    more:(ts:(-ws barToken -ws t:intersectionOrHigher)+)* !(-ws barToken)
    -> foldl($f, $more, (acc, m) => new UnionType{Types: concat(list($acc), map($m.ts, (x) => $x.t))})
def intersectionOrHigher: TypeNode = (u:leadingIntersectionType / u:plainOrIntersectionType) -> $u
def leadingIntersectionType: IntersectionType = ampersandToken -ws f:typeOperatorOrHigher
    r:(-ws ampersandToken -ws t:typeOperatorOrHigher)* !(-ws ampersandToken)
    -> new IntersectionType{Types: concat(list($f), map($r, (x) => $x.t))}
def plainOrIntersectionType: TypeNode = f:typeOperatorOrHigher
    more:(ts:(-ws ampersandToken -ws t:typeOperatorOrHigher)+)* !(-ws ampersandToken)
    -> foldl($f, $more, (acc, m) => new IntersectionType{Types: concat(list($acc), map($m.ts, (x) => $x.t))})

def typeOperatorOrHigher: TypeNode = (&(("keyof" / "unique" / "readonly" / "infer") !idPart)
    t:(typeOperator / inferType) / !(("keyof" / "unique" / "readonly" / "infer") !idPart) t:postfixTypeAllowConditional)
    -> $t
def postfixTypeAllowConditional: TypeNode = [ctx = ctx - ctx / 32 % 2 * 32] t:postfixType -> $t
def typeOperator: TypeOperator = o:@(("keyof" / "unique" / "readonly") !idPart) -ws t:typeOperatorOrHigher
    -> new TypeOperator{Operator: text($o), Type: $t}
def inferType: InferType = "infer" !idPart -ws p:inferTypeParameter -> new InferType{TypeParameter: $p}
// infer T extends C: the constraint is kept unless a conditional type may follow and "?" does.
def inferTypeParameter: TypeParameter = n:identifier
    (-ws "extends" !idPart -ws ct:typeNoConditional ([ctx / 32 % 2 == 1] / !(-ws "?")))?
    -> new TypeParameter{Name: $n, Constraint: $ct}

// Array types, indexed access types and the JSDoc postfixes ! and ?, on the same line.
def postfixType: TypeNode = pratt {
    skip (&(? \t\v\f\u{A0}\u0085\u{1680}\u{2000}-\u{200B}\u{202F}\u{205F}\u{3000}\u{FEFF}/) sp)
    operand nonArrayType
    level {
        postfix "[" -ws "]" -> new ArrayType{ElementType: $lhs}
        postfix "[" -ws &typeStart i:typeNode -ws "]" -> new IndexedAccessType{ObjectType: $lhs, IndexType: $i}
        postfix "!" !"=" -> new JSDocNonNullableType{Type: $lhs, Postfix: true}
        postfix "?" !"?" !("." !(?0-9)) !(-ws typeStart) -> new JSDocNullableType{Type: $lhs, Postfix: true}
    }
}
// The same without the postfix ?, for the optional elements of tuples.
def postfixTypeNoQuestion: TypeNode = pratt {
    skip (&(? \t\v\f\u{A0}\u0085\u{1680}\u{2000}-\u{200B}\u{202F}\u{205F}\u{3000}\u{FEFF}/) sp)
    operand nonArrayType
    level {
        postfix "[" -ws "]" -> new ArrayType{ElementType: $lhs}
        postfix "[" -ws &typeStart i:typeNode -ws "]" -> new IndexedAccessType{ObjectType: $lhs, IndexType: $i}
        postfix "!" !"=" -> new JSDocNonNullableType{Type: $lhs, Postfix: true}
    }
}

// parseNonArrayType
// The first character tells words, whose alternatives are tried in the compiler's order, from the rest.
def nonArrayType: TypeNode = (&(?a-zA-Z$_\\\u{80}-\u{10FFFF}) t:wordType / t:symbolType)
    #error(message="expected a type") -> $t
// A word that is not one of those of the other types (keywords, literals, this, typeof, import, asserts, function)
// is a type reference.
def wordType: TypeNode = (&(("any" / "unknown" / "string" / "number" / "bigint" / "symbol" / "boolean" / "undefined"
        / "never" / "object" / "void" / "true" / "false" / "null" / "this" / "typeof" / "import" / "asserts" / "function")
        !idPart) t:specialWordType / t:typeReference) -> $t
def specialWordType: TypeNode = keywordType / literalType / thisTypePredicate / thisType / importType / typeQuery
    / assertsTypePredicate / jsdocFunctionType / functionTypeReference / typeReference
def symbolType: TypeNode = literalType / mappedType / typeLiteral / tupleType / parenthesizedType
    / templateLiteralType / jsdocAllType / jsdocUnknownType / jsdocNullableType / jsdocNonNullableType / typeReference
// A keyword type, unless followed by "." (then it is a type reference)
def keywordType: KeywordTypeNode = ("any" / "unknown" / "string" / "number" / "bigint" / "symbol" / "boolean"
    / "undefined" / "never" / "object") !idPart !(-ws ".")
    / "void" !idPart
def literalType: LiteralType = l:(stringLiteral / numericLiteral / bigIntLiteral / booleanKeyword / nullKeyword
    / noSubstitutionTemplateLiteral / negativeLiteral) -> new LiteralType{Literal: $l}
def negativeLiteral: PrefixUnaryExpression = "-" -ws l:(numericLiteral / bigIntLiteral)
    -> new PrefixUnaryExpression{Operator: "-", Operand: $l}
def thisType: ThisTypeNode = "this" !idPart
def thisTypePredicate: TypePredicate = n:thisType -sp "is" !idPart -ws t:typeNode
    -> new TypePredicate{ParameterName: $n, Type: $t}
// asserts x, asserts x is T, asserts this
def assertsTypePredicate: TypePredicate = a:assertsToken &(sp identifierOrKeywordStart) -sp
    n:(thisType / identifier) (-ws "is" !idPart -ws ty:typeNode)?
    -> new TypePredicate{AssertsModifier: $a, ParameterName: $n, Type: $ty}
def assertsToken: Token = "asserts" !idPart
def identifierOrKeywordStart = idStart / "#"
def typeQuery: TypeQuery = "typeof" !idPart -ws n:entityNameAllowReserved (-sp t:typeArguments)?
    -> new TypeQuery{ExprName: $n, TypeArguments: concat($t)}
def importType: ImportType = o:("typeof" !idPart -ws)? "import" !idPart -ws "(" -ws a:typeNode
    (-ws "," -ws "{" -ws ("with" / "assert") !idPart -ws ":" -ws i:importTypeAttributes (-ws ",")? -ws "}")? -ws ")"
    (-ws "." -ws qn:entityNameAllowReserved)? (-sp t:typeArguments)?
    -> new ImportType{Argument: $a, Attributes: $i, Qualifier: $qn, TypeArguments: concat($t), IsTypeOf: $o != nil}
def importTypeAttributes: ImportAttributes = a:importAttributesBraces -> new ImportAttributes{Elements: $a, Token: "with"}
// Type arguments start at a "<" on the same line, and must follow then.
def typeReference: TypeReference = !(("typeof" / "void" / "this" / "import" / "true" / "false" / "null" / "keyof"
        / "unique" / "readonly" / "infer" / "new" / "function") !idPart) !("asserts" !idPart sp identifierOrKeywordStart)
    n:entityNameAllowReserved (-ws "." &(-sp "<"))? (-sp t:typeArguments / !(-sp "<"))
    -> new TypeReference{TypeName: $n, TypeArguments: concat($t)}
def functionTypeReference: TypeReference = n:functionIdentifier !(-ws "(") -> new TypeReference{TypeName: $n}
def functionIdentifier: Identifier = "function" !idPart
def parenthesizedType: ParenthesizedType = !unambiguousFunctionTypeStart "(" -ws t:typeNode -ws ")"
    -> new ParenthesizedType{Type: $t}
// "(" before ")", "...", or a parameter name (after modifiers) before ":", ",", "?", "=" or ") =>"
def unambiguousFunctionTypeStart = "(" -ws (")" / "..."
    / typeMemberModifiers (identifier / "this" !idPart / bindingPattern) -ws ((?:,?=) / ")" -ws "=>"))
def templateLiteralType: TemplateLiteralType = h:templateHead ss:templateTypeSpans
    -> new TemplateLiteralType{Head: $h, TemplateSpans: $ss}
def templateTypeSpans = ms:(-ws m:templateTypeSpanMiddle)* -ws t:templateTypeSpanTail
    -> concat(map($ms, (x) => $x.m), list($t))
def templateTypeSpanMiddle: TemplateLiteralTypeSpan = t:typeNode -ws l:templateMiddle
    -> new TemplateLiteralTypeSpan{Type: $t, Literal: $l}
def templateTypeSpanTail: TemplateLiteralTypeSpan = t:typeNode -ws l:templateTail
    -> new TemplateLiteralTypeSpan{Type: $t, Literal: $l}

// JSDoc types, which the parser accepts in .ts files (the checker reports them)
def jsdocAllType: JSDocAllType = "*" !"*"
def jsdocUnknownType: JSDocUnknownType = "?" &(-ws (?,}\)>=|))
def jsdocNullableType: JSDocNullableType = "?" -ws t:typeNode -> new JSDocNullableType{Type: $t}
def jsdocNonNullableType: JSDocNonNullableType = "!" -ws t:nonArrayType -> new JSDocNonNullableType{Type: $t}
def jsdocFunctionType: JSDocFunctionType = "function" !idPart -ws "(" -ws ps:jsdocParameterList?
    -ws ")" rt:returnType? -> new JSDocFunctionType{Parameters: concat($ps), Type: $rt}
def jsdocParameter: Parameter = (i:jsdocParameterName -ws ":" -ws)? t:typeNode -> new Parameter{Name: $i, Type: $t}
def jsdocParameterName: Identifier = ("this" / "new") !idPart

def entityName: EntityName = first:identifier rest:(-ws "." -ws n:identifier)*
    -> foldl($first, $rest, (acc, r) => new QualifiedName{Left: $acc, Right: $r.n})
def entityNameAllowReserved: EntityName = first:identifierNameOrPrivate rest:(-ws "." -ws n:identifierName)*
    -> foldl($first, $rest, (acc, r) => new QualifiedName{Left: $acc, Right: $r.n})

def typeArguments = "<" -ws ts:typeList? -ws ">" -> concat($ts)
// Each type starts as a type does (isListElement for TypeArguments): A<class> is an error.
def typeList = &typeStart first:typeNode rest:(-ws "," -ws &typeStart t:typeNode)* (-ws ",")?
    -> concat(list($first), map($rest, (r) => $r.t))
def typeParameters = "<" -ws ps:typeParameterList? -ws ">"
    -> concat($ps)
// The constraint is an expression when it starts an expression but no type (as in JSDoc, which the parser
// accepts here too).
def typeParameter: TypeParameter = m:typeParameterModifiers n:identifier
    (-ws "extends" !idPart -ws (&(typeStart / !expressionStart) ct:typeNode / !typeStart ex:unaryExpression))?
    (-ws "=" !(?=>) -ws dt:typeNode)?
    -> new TypeParameter{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, Constraint: $ct, Default: $dt, Expression: $ex}

// --- Tuples ---
def tupleType: TupleType = "[" -ws es:tupleElementList? -ws "]"
    -> new TupleType{Elements: concat($es)}
def tupleElement: TypeNode = namedTupleMember / tupleElementType
def namedTupleMember: NamedTupleMember = (dt:dotDotDotToken -ws)? n:identifierNameOrPrivate (-ws qt:questionToken)? -ws ":"
    -ws t:tupleElementType -> new NamedTupleMember{DotDotDotToken: $dt, Name: $n, QuestionToken: $qt, Type: $t}
// T? before "," or "]" is an optional element (the parser turns a postfix JSDocNullableType into it).
def tupleElementType: TypeNode = restType / optionalType / typeNode
def restType: RestType = "..." -ws t:typeNode -> new RestType{Type: $t}
def optionalType: OptionalType = t:postfixTypeNoQuestion -sp "?" &(-ws (?,\])) -> new OptionalType{Type: $t}

// --- Object types ---
def typeLiteral: TypeLiteral = !mappedTypeStart m:objectTypeMembers -> new TypeLiteral{Members: $m}
def objectTypeMembers = "{" -ws ms:(&typeMemberStart m:typeMember -ws)* "}" -> map($ms, (x) => $x.m)
// isTypeMemberStart: "(", "<", get, set, "[" after modifiers, or a name (or a modifier taken for one) before
// "(", "<", "?", ":", "," or a statement terminator.
def typeMemberStart = (?(<) / ("get" / "set") !idPart
    / (modifierKeyword -ws)* "["
    / (modifierKeyword -ws)* literalPropertyNameToken typeMemberNameFollows
    / modifierKeyword (-ws modifierKeyword)* typeMemberNameFollows
def typeMemberNameFollows = nlAhead / -ws ((?(<?:,;}) / $$)
def literalPropertyNameToken = identifierName / privateIdentifier / stringLiteral / numericLiteral / bigIntLiteral
// isStartOfMappedType
def mappedTypeStart = "{" -ws ((?+\-) -ws "readonly" !idPart / ("readonly" !idPart -ws)? "[" -ws identifier -ws "in" !idPart)
def mappedType: MappedType = &mappedTypeStart "{" -ws (rt:mappedReadonlyToken -ws)? "[" -ws p:mappedTypeParameter
    (-ws "as" !idPart -ws nt:typeNode)? -ws "]" (-ws qt:mappedQuestionToken)? t:typeAnnotation? eos -ws
    ms:(&typeMemberStart m:typeMember -ws)* "}"
    -> new MappedType{ReadonlyToken: $rt, TypeParameter: $p, NameType: $nt, QuestionToken: $qt, Type: $t,
        Members: map($ms, (x) => $x.m)}
def mappedTypeParameter: TypeParameter = n:identifierNameOrPrivate -ws "in" !idPart -ws c:typeNode
    -> new TypeParameter{Name: $n, Constraint: $c}
def mappedReadonlyToken: Token = t:(mappedPlusMinusReadonly / readonlyToken) -> $t
def mappedPlusMinusReadonly: Token = t:plusMinusToken -ws "readonly" !idPart -> $t
def mappedQuestionToken: Token = t:(mappedPlusMinusQuestion / questionToken) -> $t
def mappedPlusMinusQuestion: Token = t:plusMinusToken -ws "?" -> $t
def plusMinusToken: Token = (?+\-)
def readonlyToken: Token = "readonly" !idPart

// parseTypeMember
def typeMember: TypeElement = callSignature / constructSignature / typeAccessor / typeMemberNotAccessor
def typeAccessor: TypeElement = &(typeMemberModifiers accessorKeyword) m:(typeGetAccessor / typeSetAccessor) -> $m
def typeMemberNotAccessor: TypeElement = !(typeMemberModifiers accessorKeyword)
    m:(typeIndexSignature / methodSignature / propertySignature) -> $m
def callSignature: CallSignature = (t:typeParameters -ws)? ps:parameterList rt:returnType? typeMemberSemicolon
    -> new CallSignature{TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps, Type: $rt}
def constructSignature: ConstructSignature = "new" !idPart -ws &(?(<) (t:typeParameters -ws)? ps:parameterList
    rt:returnType? typeMemberSemicolon -> new ConstructSignature{TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps, Type: $rt}
def typeGetAccessor: GetAccessor = m:typeMemberModifiers "get" !idPart &(-ws canFollowGetOrSet) -ws n:propertyName
    (-ws t:typeParameters)? -ws ps:parameterList rt:returnType? (-ws fb:block / !(-ws "{") typeMemberSemicolon)
    -> new GetAccessor{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps, Type: $rt, Body: $fb}
def typeSetAccessor: SetAccessor = m:typeMemberModifiers "set" !idPart &(-ws canFollowGetOrSet) -ws n:propertyName
    (-ws t:typeParameters)? -ws ps:parameterList rt:returnType? (-ws fb:block / !(-ws "{") typeMemberSemicolon)
    -> new SetAccessor{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps, Type: $rt, Body: $fb}
def typeIndexSignature: IndexSignature = m:typeMemberModifiers &indexSignatureStart "[" -ws ps:parameters? -ws "]"
    t:typeAnnotation? typeMemberSemicolon -> new IndexSignature{Modifiers: $m, Parameters: concat($ps), Type: $t}
// isUnambiguouslyIndexSignature
def indexSignatureStart = "[" -ws ("..." / "]" / modifierKeyword -ws identifier
    / identifier -ws ((?:,) / "?" -ws (?:,\])))
def modifierKeyword = ("abstract" / "accessor" / "async" / "const" / "declare" / "default" / "export" / "in" / "out"
    / "override" / "private" / "protected" / "public" / "readonly" / "static") !idPart
def methodSignature: MethodSignature = m:typeMemberModifiers n:propertyName (-ws qt:questionToken)? -ws &(?(<)
    (t:typeParameters -ws)? ps:parameterList rt:returnType? typeMemberSemicolon
    -> new MethodSignature{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, QuestionToken: $qt, TypeParameters: concat($t), Parameters: $ps,
        Type: $rt}
def propertySignature: PropertySignature = m:typeMemberModifiers n:propertyName (-ws qt:questionToken)?
    t:typeAnnotation? i:initializer? typeMemberSemicolon
    -> new PropertySignature{Modifiers: $m, Name: $n, QuestionToken: $qt, Type: $t, Initializer: $i}
// "," or a statement terminator (parseTypeMemberSemicolon)
def typeMemberSemicolon = -ws "," / eos

// isStartOfType (used where "?" might be a postfix type operator)
// (Like declarationStart, a lookahead that recurses after "(".)
def typeStart = ("any" / "unknown" / "string" / "number" / "bigint" / "boolean" / "readonly" / "symbol" / "unique"
        / "void" / "undefined" / "null" / "this" / "typeof" / "never" / "true" / "false" / "object" / "new"
        / "infer" / "import" / "asserts" / "function") !idPart
    / (?{[<|&"'0-9*?!`) / "..." / "." (?0-9)
    / "-" -ws ((?0-9) / "." (?0-9))
    / "(" -ws ((?\)[{@.#) / modifierKeyword / typeStart / bindingIdentifier)
    / !reservedWord idStart

// ===================================================================
// Names and literals
// ===================================================================

def propertyName: PropertyName = stringLiteral / numericLiteral / bigIntLiteral / computedPropertyName
    / privateIdentifier / identifierName
def computedPropertyName: ComputedPropertyName = "[" -ws e:expressionAllowIn -ws "]"
    -> new ComputedPropertyName{Expression: $e}

// --- Tokens ---
def questionToken: Token = "?"
def exclamationToken: Token = "!" !"="
def asteriskToken: Token = "*"
def dotDotDotToken: Token = "..."
def equalsGreaterThanToken: Token = "=>"
def colonToken: Token = ":"
def equalsToken: Token = "=" !(?=>)
def commaToken: Token = ","

// --- Identifiers ---
// An identifier is not a reserved word, nor yield in the yield context or await in the await context
// (isIdentifier). A binding identifier may be yield or await (isBindingIdentifier).
def identifier: Identifier = !(&(?bcdefinrstvw) reservedWord) !("yield" !idPart [ctx % 2 == 1]) !("await" !idPart [ctx / 2 % 2 == 1])
    i:identifierName -> $i
def bindingIdentifier: Identifier = !(&(?bcdefinrstvw) reservedWord) i:identifierName -> $i
def identifierName: Identifier = ((?a-zA-Z$_) / idStartOther) identifierRest
def privateIdentifier: PrivateIdentifier = "#" ((?a-zA-Z$_) / idStartOther) identifierRest
def identifierNameOrPrivate: Identifier = "#"? ((?a-zA-Z$_) / idStartOther) identifierRest
// Every keyword, reserved or contextual
def anyKeyword = ("abstract" / "accessor" / "any" / "asserts" / "assert" / "async" / "as" / "await" / "bigint"
    / "boolean" / "break" / "case" / "catch" / "class" / "constructor" / "const" / "continue" / "debugger"
    / "declare" / "default" / "defer" / "delete" / "do" / "else" / "enum" / "export" / "extends" / "false"
    / "finally" / "for" / "from" / "function" / "get" / "global" / "if" / "implements" / "import" / "infer"
    / "instanceof" / "interface" / "intrinsic" / "in" / "is" / "keyof" / "let" / "module" / "namespace" / "never"
    / "new" / "null" / "number" / "object" / "of" / "out" / "override" / "package" / "private" / "protected"
    / "public" / "readonly" / "require" / "return" / "satisfies" / "set" / "static" / "string" / "super"
    / "switch" / "symbol" / "this" / "throw" / "true" / "try" / "typeof" / "type" / "undefined" / "unique"
    / "unknown" / "using" / "var" / "void" / "while" / "with" / "yield") !idPart
// The first letter selects the words to try.
def reservedWord = (&"b" "break" / &"c" ("case" / "catch" / "class" / "const" / "continue")
    / &"d" ("debugger" / "default" / "delete" / "do") / &"e" ("else" / "enum" / "export" / "extends")
    / &"f" ("false" / "finally" / "for" / "function") / &"i" ("if" / "import" / "instanceof" / "in")
    / &"n" ("new" / "null") / &"r" "return" / &"s" ("super" / "switch")
    / &"t" ("this" / "throw" / "true" / "try" / "typeof") / &"v" ("var" / "void") / &"w" ("while" / "with")) !idPart
// The rest of an identifier: runs of ASCII identifier characters, which are most of them, without a rule call
// per character, and the escapes and non-ASCII characters between them.
def identifierRest = (?a-zA-Z0-9$_)* (&(?\\\u{80}-\u{10FFFF}) ("\\u" identifierPartEscape / uniIdPart) (?a-zA-Z0-9$_)*)*
def idStart = (?a-zA-Z$_) / idStartOther
def idStartOther = "\\u" identifierStartEscape / uniIdStart
def idPart = (?a-zA-Z0-9$_) / "\\u" identifierPartEscape / uniIdPart
// An escape in an identifier stands for an identifier character: exactly for ASCII values; any value from
// U+0080 is accepted (the Unicode tables are not applied to escapes).
def identifierStartEscape = "00" asciiIdentifierStartHex / !"00" !surrogate hex hex hex hex / "00" (?89a-fA-F) hex
    / "{" "0"* (asciiIdentifierStartHex "}" / nonASCIIBraced)
def identifierPartEscape = "00" (asciiIdentifierStartHex / "3" (?0-9)) / !"00" !surrogate hex hex hex hex / "00" (?89a-fA-F) hex
    / "{" "0"* (asciiIdentifierStartHex "}" / "3" (?0-9) "}" / nonASCIIBraced)
def surrogate = (?dD) (?89a-fA-F)
// $, A-Z, _, a-z
def asciiIdentifierStartHex = "24" / "4" (?1-9a-fA-F) / "5" (?0-9aA) / "5" (?fF) / "6" (?1-9a-fA-F) / "7" (?0-9aA)
// 80 to 10FFFF, after leading zeros
def nonASCIIBraced = (?89a-fA-F) hex "}" / (?1-9a-fA-F) hex hex hex? hex? "}" / "10" hex hex hex hex "}"
def unicodeEscape = hex hex hex hex / unicodeBraced
// \u{...} with a value up to 10FFFF
def unicodeBraced = "{" ("0"* (?1-9a-fA-F) hex? hex? hex? hex? "}" / "0"* "10" hex hex hex hex "}" / "0"+ "}")
def hex = (?0-9a-fA-F)

// --- Numbers (scanNumber) ---
// A literal may not be followed by an identifier; 0 may not be followed by a digit (no legacy octal
// literals, no decimals with leading zeros).
def numericLiteral: NumericLiteral = (hexLiteral / binaryLiteral / octalLiteral / decimalLiteral) !idStart
def bigIntLiteral: BigIntLiteral = (hexLiteral / binaryLiteral / octalLiteral / decimalInteger) "n" !idStart
def decimalLiteral = decimalInteger ("." decimalDigits?)? exponentPart? / "." decimalDigits exponentPart?
def decimalInteger = "0" !(?0-9_) / (?1-9) ("_"? (?0-9))*
def decimalDigits = (?0-9) ("_"? (?0-9))*
def exponentPart = (?eE) (?+\-)? decimalDigits
def hexLiteral = "0" (?xX) hex ("_"? hex)*
def binaryLiteral = "0" (?bB) (?01) ("_"? (?01))*
def octalLiteral = "0" (?oO) (?0-7) ("_"? (?0-7))*

// --- Strings (scanString, scanEscapeSequence) ---
// Octal escapes, \8 and \9 are errors; \0 is allowed when no digit follows.
def stringLiteral: StringLiteral = "\"" ((?^"\\\n\r)+ / escapeSequence)* "\"" / "'" ((?^'\\\n\r)+ / escapeSequence)* "'"
def escapeSequence = "\\" ((?^0-9xu\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}) / "0" !(?0-9) / "x" hex hex / "u" unicodeEscape / "\r\n"
    / (?\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}))

// --- Templates (scanTemplateAndSetTokenValue) ---
def noSubstitutionTemplateLiteral: NoSubstitutionTemplateLiteral = "`" templateCharacters "`"
def templateHead: TemplateHead = "`" templateCharacters "${"
def templateMiddle: TemplateMiddle = "}" templateCharacters "${"
def templateTail: TemplateTail = "}" templateCharacters "`"
def templateCharacters = ((?^`\\$)+ / "$" !"{" / escapeSequence)*
def rawNoSubstitutionTemplateLiteral: NoSubstitutionTemplateLiteral = "`" rawTemplateCharacters "`"
def rawTemplateHead: TemplateHead = "`" rawTemplateCharacters "${"
def rawTemplateMiddle: TemplateMiddle = "}" rawTemplateCharacters "${"
def rawTemplateTail: TemplateTail = "}" rawTemplateCharacters "`"
def rawTemplateCharacters = ((?^`\\$)+ / "$" !"{" / "\\" .)*

// --- Regular expressions (reScanSlashToken) ---
// The body up to an unescaped "/" outside a class, on one line, and any identifier characters as flags;
// the parser does not check the pattern or the flags.
def regularExpressionLiteral: RegularExpressionLiteral = "/" !(?*/) ((?^/\\[\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029})+
    / "\\" (?^\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}) / "[" ((?^\]\\\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029})+ / "\\" (?^\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}))* "]")+ "/" ((?a-zA-Z0-9$_) / uniIdPart)*

// --- Whitespace and comments ---
// The whitespace characters of isWhiteSpaceSingleLine, and the line terminators of isLineBreak. Most calls find
// none, so a silent test of the next character comes first (it must include "/", the start of a comment).
def ws = (&(? \t\n\r\v\f\u{A0}\u0085\u{1680}\u{2000}-\u{200B}\u{2028}\u{2029}\u{202F}\u{205F}\u{3000}\u{FEFF}/)
    ((? \t\n\r\v\f\u{A0}\u0085\u{1680}\u{2000}-\u{200B}\u{2028}\u{2029}\u{202F}\u{205F}\u{3000}\u{FEFF})+
    / "//" (?^\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029})* / "/*" (!"*/" .)* "*/"))*
def sp = (&(? \t\v\f\u{A0}\u0085\u{1680}\u{2000}-\u{200B}\u{202F}\u{205F}\u{3000}\u{FEFF}/)
    ((? \t\v\f\u{A0}\u0085\u{1680}\u{2000}-\u{200B}\u{202F}\u{205F}\u{3000}\u{FEFF})+
    / "//" (?^\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029})* / "/*" (!"*/" (?^\n\r\u{2028}\u{2029}))* "*/"))*

// Comma-separated lists, with an optional trailing comma
def arrayBindingElementList = f:arrayBindingElement r:(-ws "," -ws e:arrayBindingElement)* (-ws ",")? -> concat(list($f), map($r, (x) => $x.e))
def arrayElementList = f:arrayElement r:(-ws "," -ws e:arrayElement)* (-ws ",")? -> concat(list($f), map($r, (x) => $x.e))
def bindingElementList = f:bindingElement r:(-ws "," -ws e:bindingElement)* (-ws ",")? -> concat(list($f), map($r, (x) => $x.e))
def enumMemberList = f:enumMember r:(-ws "," -ws e:enumMember)* (-ws ",")? -> concat(list($f), map($r, (x) => $x.e))
def exportSpecifierList = f:exportSpecifier r:(-ws "," -ws e:exportSpecifier)* (-ws ",")? -> concat(list($f), map($r, (x) => $x.e))
def importAttributeList = f:importAttribute r:(-ws "," -ws e:importAttribute)* (-ws ",")? -> concat(list($f), map($r, (x) => $x.e))
def importSpecifierList = f:importSpecifier r:(-ws "," -ws e:importSpecifier)* (-ws ",")? -> concat(list($f), map($r, (x) => $x.e))
def jsdocParameterList = f:jsdocParameter r:(-ws "," -ws p:jsdocParameter)* -> concat(list($f), map($r, (x) => $x.p))
def jsxAttributeLikeList = f:jsxAttributeLike r:(-ws a:jsxAttributeLike)* -> concat(list($f), map($r, (x) => $x.a))
def objectLiteralElementList = &objectLiteralElementStart f:objectLiteralElement
    r:(-ws "," -ws &objectLiteralElementStart e:objectLiteralElement)* (-ws ",")? -> concat(list($f), map($r, (x) => $x.e))
def tupleElementList = &typeStart f:tupleElement r:(-ws "," -ws &typeStart e:tupleElement)* (-ws ",")? -> concat(list($f), map($r, (x) => $x.e))
def typeParameterList = &typeParameterStart f:typeParameter r:(-ws "," -ws &typeParameterStart p:typeParameter)* (-ws ",")?
    -> concat(list($f), map($r, (x) => $x.p))
def typeParameterStart = ("in" / "const") !idPart / identifier

// Unicode ID_Start and ID_Continue beyond ASCII, as TypeScript's tables have them (unicodeESNextIdentifierStart
// and unicodeESNextIdentifierPart); the first class rejects ASCII quickly.
def uniIdStart = &(?\u{80}-\u{10FFFF}) (?\u{AA}\u{B5}\u{BA}\u{C0}-\u{D6}\u{D8}-\u{F6}\u{F8}-\u{2C1}\u{2C6}-\u{2D1}\u{2E0}-\u{2E4}\u{2EC}\u{2EE}\u{370}-\u{374}\u{376}-\u{377}\u{37A}-\u{37D}\u{37F}\u{386}\u{388}-\u{38A}\u{38C}\u{38E}-\u{3A1}\u{3A3}-\u{3F5}\u{3F7}-\u{481}\u{48A}-\u{52F}\u{531}-\u{556}\u{559}\u{560}-\u{588}\u{5D0}-\u{5EA}\u{5EF}-\u{5F2}\u{620}-\u{64A}\u{66E}-\u{66F}\u{671}-\u{6D3}\u{6D5}\u{6E5}-\u{6E6}\u{6EE}-\u{6EF}\u{6FA}-\u{6FC}\u{6FF}\u{710}\u{712}-\u{72F}\u{74D}-\u{7A5}\u{7B1}\u{7CA}-\u{7EA}\u{7F4}-\u{7F5}\u{7FA}\u{800}-\u{815}\u{81A}\u{824}\u{828}\u{840}-\u{858}\u{860}-\u{86A}\u{870}-\u{887}\u{889}-\u{88E}\u{8A0}-\u{8C9}\u{904}-\u{939}\u{93D}\u{950}\u{958}-\u{961}\u{971}-\u{980}\u{985}-\u{98C}\u{98F}-\u{990}\u{993}-\u{9A8}\u{9AA}-\u{9B0}\u{9B2}\u{9B6}-\u{9B9}\u{9BD}\u{9CE}\u{9DC}-\u{9DD}\u{9DF}-\u{9E1}\u{9F0}-\u{9F1}\u{9FC}\u{A05}-\u{A0A}\u{A0F}-\u{A10}\u{A13}-\u{A28}\u{A2A}-\u{A30}\u{A32}-\u{A33}\u{A35}-\u{A36}\u{A38}-\u{A39}\u{A59}-\u{A5C}\u{A5E}\u{A72}-\u{A74}\u{A85}-\u{A8D}\u{A8F}-\u{A91}\u{A93}-\u{AA8}\u{AAA}-\u{AB0}\u{AB2}-\u{AB3}\u{AB5}-\u{AB9}\u{ABD}\u{AD0}\u{AE0}-\u{AE1}\u{AF9}\u{B05}-\u{B0C}\u{B0F}-\u{B10}\u{B13}-\u{B28}\u{B2A}-\u{B30}\u{B32}-\u{B33}\u{B35}-\u{B39}\u{B3D}\u{B5C}-\u{B5D}\u{B5F}-\u{B61}\u{B71}\u{B83}\u{B85}-\u{B8A}\u{B8E}-\u{B90}\u{B92}-\u{B95}\u{B99}-\u{B9A}\u{B9C}\u{B9E}-\u{B9F}\u{BA3}-\u{BA4}\u{BA8}-\u{BAA}\u{BAE}-\u{BB9}\u{BD0}\u{C05}-\u{C0C}\u{C0E}-\u{C10}\u{C12}-\u{C28}\u{C2A}-\u{C39}\u{C3D}\u{C58}-\u{C5A}\u{C5D}\u{C60}-\u{C61}\u{C80}\u{C85}-\u{C8C}\u{C8E}-\u{C90}\u{C92}-\u{CA8}\u{CAA}-\u{CB3}\u{CB5}-\u{CB9}\u{CBD}\u{CDD}-\u{CDE}\u{CE0}-\u{CE1}\u{CF1}-\u{CF2}\u{D04}-\u{D0C}\u{D0E}-\u{D10}\u{D12}-\u{D3A}\u{D3D}\u{D4E}\u{D54}-\u{D56}\u{D5F}-\u{D61}\u{D7A}-\u{D7F}\u{D85}-\u{D96}\u{D9A}-\u{DB1}\u{DB3}-\u{DBB}\u{DBD}\u{DC0}-\u{DC6}\u{E01}-\u{E30}\u{E32}-\u{E33}\u{E40}-\u{E46}\u{E81}-\u{E82}\u{E84}\u{E86}-\u{E8A}\u{E8C}-\u{EA3}\u{EA5}\u{EA7}-\u{EB0}\u{EB2}-\u{EB3}\u{EBD}\u{EC0}-\u{EC4}\u{EC6}\u{EDC}-\u{EDF}\u{F00}\u{F40}-\